{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HvgXurtrHZaL9ZfWo6GV6E","type":"tool_result","content":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Ret\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's facing; exposure is the share of three points on it (its feet, its chest,\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1458:- `grid.threat(units, o = {})`: what a side can strike on its next turn: units ([{ cx, cy, move, range: [min, max] or n (1), climb, drop }]) each moving within its reach (o.blocked: cells it can't enter) and striking within range of where it stops. { cells: [[cx, cy, n]], count(c), by(c) -> [un\n....\n// my-3D2dge game checker: loads a game in a headless browser, presses start, plays it for a\n// moment, switches through the game's camera views, and reports errors, warnings, frame rate,\n// how much of the window the picture covers (covers: 1 = no black bars), how much is actually on screen, and screenshots.\n//\n// Setup (once):   npm install          (installs Playwright)\n//                 npx playwright install chromium\n// Usage:          node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html[#scene] [--seconds 4] [--out check-output] [--size 390x844@3]\n//                 (--size: the window in CSS pixels and its pixel density; @2 and up is a phone or tablet, with touch)\n// Exit code is 1 if the page threw any error or never drew anything, so agents and CI can rely on it.\n// A game that sets game.debug = { snapshot() { return {...} } } gets its snapshot printed after play (its own state:\n// the hero, the objective, what an agent needs to see the game is where it should be).\n\nconst args = process.argv.slice(2);\nconst file = args.find(a => !a.startsWith('--') && !/^\\d+(\\.\\d+)?$/.test(a));\nconst opt = (name, def) => { const i = args.indexOf('--' + name); return i >= 0 ? args[i + 1] : def; };\nif (!file) { console.error('Usage: node tools/check.mjs path/to/game.html [--seconds 4] [--out check-output]'); process.exit(2); }\nconst seconds = +opt('seconds', 4), out = resolve(opt('out', 'check-output'));\nconst [, sw, sh, sd] = (opt('size', '1280x720') || '').match(/^(\\d+)x(\\d+)(?:@(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?))?$/) || [0, 1280, 720];\nconst dpr = +(sd || 1), size = { viewport: { width: +sw, height: +sh }, deviceScaleFactor: dpr, ...(dpr >= 2 && { isMobile: true, hasTouch: true }) };\nmkdirSync(out, { recursive: true });\n\nconst browser = await chromium.launch({ executablePath: process.env.CHROMIUM_PATH || undefined, args: ['--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required'] });\nconst page = await browser.newPage(size);\nconst errors = [], warnings = [], engineWarnings = [], external = new Set();\npage.on('pageerror', e => errors.push(String(e && e.stack || e)));\npage.on('console', m => {\n  const t = m.text();\n  if (m.type() === 'error') errors.push(t);\n  else if (m.type() === 'warning') (t.startsWith('my-3D2dge:') ? engineWarnings : warnings).push(t);\n});\npage.on('request', r => { const u = r.url(); if (/^https?:/i.test(u)) external.add(u.split('?')[0]); });\n\n// a #hash after the file name is kept, so deep links like game.html#platformer work\nconst [filePath, hash] = file.split('#');\nawait page.goto(pathToFileURL(resolve(filePath)).href + (hash ? '#' + hash : ''));\nawait page.waitForTimeout(1200);\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"3029b105-3bc7-45f9-9e71-08a738167252","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:57:20.085Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"42:if (E.targets(guard, [hero], { range: 60 }).length) throw new Error('not on the same level: no melee target');\n431:- `r.sightCone(obs, o = {})` †: an observer's view on the ground: a dithered fan fov wide (radians) about its facing, out to range, cut short where the map hides a body's chest (map.ray, the height rules), draped over the ground below. o: { range: 120, fov: 1.6, facing, map, eye, color: '#ffe080\n565:- `settings.define(sp)`: add a setting: { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', value, min, max, step, options: [[value, label]] or [value], help, group: 'Game', apply(game, value) }. Its saved value is loaded (when it is a valid one) and applied; it shows on the settings screen. Ret\n568:- `settings.set(key, v)`: change a setting: checked (a slider kept in range, a choice among its options), saved, applied, onChange told. Returns the value kept (the old one when v is not a valid value)\n1015:- `E.sees(obs, tgt, o = {})`: can observer see target? { seen, d (ground distance), angle (observer -> target), exposure: 0..1 }. The target must be within range and inside the cone fov wide (radians) about the observer's fac