{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014n1FGhnyM5bn2ihtsqNeHs","type":"tool_result","content":"- **Spray:** `θ = −(e / window) · 48° + ((bx − rx) / r) · 10° + noise(±4°)` for a right-handed batter (early pulls\n  to left field); mirrored for lefties. |θ| > 45° is foul.\n- **Launch:** `φ = 12° − ((rz − bz) / r) · 35°`. Swinging above the ball (the reticle higher than the ball) drives a\n  grounder; swinging under it lofts a fly. A power swing adds +6°; a Batzooka swing clamps φ to 28°–38°.\n- **Exit speed:** `EV = lerp(220, EVmax, Q^1.3) × Power stat (0.85–1.15) × (0.9 + 0.1 · pitchSpeed / 340) ×\n  TUNE.exitVelocity × park.evMul`.\n- **Velocity:** `vx = EV cos φ sin θ`, `vy = −EV cos φ cos θ`, `vz = EV sin φ`. Sidespin = −e · 3 (late swings slice\n  away).\n- **Feedback** (on for Rookie, Training and the \"Timing feedback\" setting): \"EARLY 34 ms\", \"PERFECT!\", \"LATE 12 ms\",\n----\n- **Starts** after **10 s with no input** on the title or the top-level menus (mode select, Team Select before anyone\n  joins, Derby Setup, lesson list, About). Input means any key, button, click, touch, stick past the dead zone, or\n  mouse movement over 4 px.\n----\n| Menus | select | back | – | – | previous tab | next tab | – | – | hover focuses, click selects |\n\n- **Mouse:** the pointer aims the bat or the pitch (pointer → zone plane by inverse-interpolating the zone's 4\n  projected corners). In the Broadcast Cam, `game.mouseGround()` within 26 U of a base hovers it. Fielding and running\n  use `input.suppressCode('Mouse0')` / `'Mouse2'` unless the click lands on a base, so a stray click never throws home.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"271a9917-b288-4364-98cf-7624b2e0a955","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:31.649Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- **Spray:** `θ = −(e / window) · 48° + ((bx − rx) / r) · 10° + noise(±4°)` for a right-handed batter (early pulls\n  to left field); mirrored for lefties. |θ| > 45° is foul.\n- **Launch:** `φ = 12° − ((rz − bz) / r) · 35°`. Swinging above the ball (the reticle higher than the ball) drives a\n  grounder; swinging under it lofts a fly. A power swing adds +6°; a Batzooka swing clamps φ to 28°–38°.\n- **Exit speed:** `EV = lerp(220, EVmax, Q^1.3) × Power stat (0.85–1.15) × (0.9 + 0.1 · pitchSpeed / 340) ×\n  TUNE.exitVelocity × park.evMul`.\n- **Velocity:** `vx = EV cos φ sin θ`, `vy = −EV cos φ cos θ`, `vz = EV sin φ`. Sidespin = −e · 3 (late swings slice\n  away).\n- **Feedback** (on for Rookie, Training and the \"Timing feedback\" setting): \"EARLY 34 ms\", \"PERFECT!\", \"LATE 12 ms\",\n----\n- **Starts** after **10 s with no input** on the title or the top-level menus (mode select, Team Select before anyone\n  joins, Derby Setup, lesson list, About). Input means any key, button, click, touch, stick past the dead zone, or\n  mouse movement over 4 px.\n----\n| Menus | select | back | – | – | previous tab | next tab | – | – | hover focuses, click selects |\n\n- **Mouse:** the pointer aims the bat or the pitch (pointer → zone plane by inverse-interpolating the zone's 4\n  projected corners). In the Broadcast Cam, `game.mouseGround()` within 26 U of a base hovers it. Fielding and running\n  use `input.suppressCode('Mouse0')` / `'Mouse2'` unless the click lands on a base, so a stray click never throws home.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014n1FGhnyM5bn2ihtsqNeHs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2bMCjvYDrcbTPUR6Li","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KFHXdWfJj7BsHgMdsZxLPf","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\nfixes = [\n # 1. spray sign: for a righty, early (e < 0) must pull to left field (θ < 0)\n (\"- **Spray:** `θ = −(e / window) · 48° + ((bx − rx) / r) · 10° + noise(±4°)` for a right-handed batter (early pulls\\n  to left field); mirrored for lefties. |θ| > 45° is foul.\",\n  \"- **Spray:** `θ = (e / window) · 48° + ((bx − rx) / r) · 10° + noise(±4°)` for a right-handed batter: early (e < 0)\\n  pulls to left field (θ < 0), late goes the other way, and an outside pitch (bx > rx) drifts toward right field.\\n  Negate the timing term for lefties (early pulls to right field). |θ| > 45° is foul.\"),\n # 2. sidespin without a sign trap\n (\"Sidespin = −e · 3 (late swings slice\\n  away).\",\n  \"Sidespin has magnitude 3 · |e| (e in\\n  seconds) and curves the ball further toward the side it was hit: late swings slice to the opposite field, early ones\\n  hook to the pull side.\"),\n # 3. Batzooka exit speed made consistent with TUNE.batzookaPower\n (\"| R1 / E, then a swing button | Batzooka (meter full; arms the next swing) | 0.16 s | 6.3 | 1,250 U/s, plus a rocket boost |\",\n  \"| R1 / E, then a swing button | Batzooka (meter full; arms the next swing) | 0.16 s | 6.3 | 780 × `TUNE.batzookaPower` (1.6) ≈ 1,250 U/s, plus a rocket boost |\"),\n (\"on contact EV ×1.6 (`TUNE.batzookaPower`), loft 28–38°\",\n  \"on contact EVmax = 780 × `TUNE.batzookaPower` (1.6, about 1,250 U/s), loft 28–38°\"),\n # 4. the iso view is already turned 45°\n (\"the replay runs at ×0.5 in the `iso` view, turned 45° (`game.rotateView`), with a \\\"REPLAY\\\" banner and a pulsing\",\n  \"the replay runs at ×0.5 in the engine's `iso` view (yaw 45, a new angle on the play), with a \\\"REPLAY\\\" banner and a pulsing\"),\n # 5. attract idle screens: there is no separate mode-select scene\n (\"on the title or the top-level menus (mode select, Team Select before anyone\\n  joins, Derby Setup, lesson list, About).\",\n  \"on the title (its mode menu included) or the other top-level menus (the Tour\\n  menu, Team Select before anyone joins, Derby Setup, the lesson list, About).\"),\n # 6. About is reached from the title only\n (\"**The About/Credits screen** (from the title; also linked from the pause menu outside sessions) has pages turned by\",\n  \"**The About/Credits screen** (from the title's ABOUT) has pages turned by\"),\n # 7. M2 done criteria include the Derby tests\n (\"- **Done when:** T-HUB passes headless and `window.__hubCheck.pass`\",\n  \"- **Done when:** T-DERBY and T-HUB pass headless and `window.__hubCheck.pass`\"),\n # 8. front-end wording\n (\"- Title, mode select, Team Select with joining (1–4), results,\",\n  \"- Title (with its mode menu), Team Select with joining (1–4), results,\"),\n # 9. modifier rule for base buttons\n (\"- **Mouse:** the pointer aims the bat or the pitch (pointer → zone plane by inverse-interpolating the zone's 4\",\n  \"- **Base buttons:** while L1 is held (batting, pitching, running) or R1 is held (running, or Laser Arm), the face\\n  buttons stop doing their usual jobs and pick a base by position: ○ first, △ second, □ third, ✕ home. Without the\\n  fielder holding the ball, nothing else uses them as bases.\\n- **Mouse:** the pointer aims the bat or the pitch (pointer → zone plane by inverse-interpolating the zone's 4\"),\n]\nfor old, new in fixes:\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == 1, (n, old[:60])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s); print('applied', len(fixes), 'fixes')\nPY","description":"Apply consistency fixes to PLAN.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":893,"cache_read_input_tokens":417870,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":893},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"f0b8e575-a02b-494b-87ec-585581a4f33d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:34:46.277Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2bLybfqFKQk9SRv7V5","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01KFHXdWfJj7BsHgMdsZxLPf":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\nfixes = [\n # 1. spray sign: for a righty, early (e < 0) must pull to left field (θ < 0)\n (\"- **Spray:** `θ = −(e / window) · 48° + ((bx − rx) / r) · 10° + noise(±4°)` for a right-handed batter (early pulls\\n  to left field); mirrored for lefties. |θ| > 45° is foul.\",\n  \"- **Spray:** `θ = (e / window) · 48° + ((bx − rx) / r) · 10° + noise(±4°)` for a right-handed batter: early (e < 0)\\n  pulls to left field (θ < 0), late goes the other way, and an outside pitch (bx > rx) drifts toward right field.\\n  Negate the timing term for lefties (early pulls to right field). |θ| > 45° is foul.\"),\n # 2. sidespin without a sign trap\n (\"Sidespin = −e · 3 (late swings slice\\n  away).\",\n  \"Sidespin has magnitude 3 · |e| (e in\\n  seconds) and curves the ball further toward the side it was hit: late swings slice to the opposite field, early ones\\n  hook to the pull side.\"),\n # 3. Batzooka exit speed made consistent with TUNE.batzookaPower\n (\"| R1 / E, then a swing button | Batzooka (meter full; arms the next swing) | 0.16 s | 6.3 | 1,250 U/s, plus a rocket boost |\",\n  \"| R1 / E, then a swing button | Batzooka (meter full; arms the next swing) | 0.16 s | 6.3 | 780 × `TUNE.batzookaPower` (1.6) ≈ 1,250 U/s, plus a rocket boost |\"),\n (\"on contact EV ×1.6 (`TUNE.batzookaPower`), loft 28–38°\",\n  \"on contact EVmax = 780 × `TUNE.batzookaPower` (1.6, about 1,250 U/s), loft 28–38°\"),\n # 4. the iso view is already turned 45°\n (\"the replay runs at ×0.5 in the `iso` view, turned 45° (`game.rotateView`), with a \\\"REPLAY\\\" banner and a pulsing\",\n  \"the replay runs at ×0.5 in the engine's `iso` view (yaw 45, a new angle on the play), with a \\\"REPLAY\\\" banner and a pulsing\"),\n # 5. attract idle screens: there is no separate mode-select scene\n (\"on the title or the top-level menus (mode select, Team Select before anyone\\n  joins, Derby Setup, lesson list, About).\",\n  \"on the title (its mode menu included) or the other top-level menus (the Tour\\n  menu, Team Select before anyone joins, Derby Setup, the lesson list, About).\"),\n # 6. About is reached from the title only\n (\"**The About/Credits screen** (from the title; also linked from the pause menu outside sessions) has pages turned by\",\n  \"**The About/Credits screen** (from the title's ABOUT) has pages turned by\"),\n # 7. M2 done criteria include the Derby tests\n (\"- **Done when:** T-HUB passes headless and `window.__hubCheck.pass`\",\n  \"- **Done when:** T-DERBY and T-HUB pass headless and `window.__hubCheck.pass`\"),\n # 8. front-end wording\n (\"- Title, mode select, Team Select with joining (1–4), results,\",\n  \"- Title (with its mode menu), Team Select with joining (1–4), results,\"),\n # 9. modifier rule for base buttons\n (\"- **Mouse:** the pointer aims the bat or the pitch (pointer → zone plane by inverse-interpolating the zone's 4\",\n  \"- **Base buttons:** while L1 is held (batting, pitching, running) or R1 is held (running, or Laser Arm), the face\\n  buttons stop doing their usual jobs and pick a base by position: ○ first, △ second, □ third, ✕ home. Without the\\n  fielder holding the ball, nothing else uses them as bases.\\n- **Mouse:** the pointer aims the bat or the pitch (pointer → zone plane by inverse-interpolating the zone's 4\"),\n]\nfor old, new in fixes:\n    n = s.count(old)\n    assert n == 1, (n, old[:60])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s); print('applied', len(fixes), 'fixes')\nPY","description":"Apply consistency fixes to PLAN.md"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01KFHXdWfJj7BsHgMdsZxLPf":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work"}}}
