{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PpshpLfYNkeG3AYb6zfv4W","type":"tool_result","content":"1167\t\n1168\t**Session rules:**\n1169\t- **No title or restart:** Quit to title, Restart, Dev Mode and Pitching Change are hidden, and the back gesture is\n1170\t  swallowed.\n1171\t- **No popups or sockets:** no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, new windows or sockets.\n1172\t- **Storage:** the client already gives an empty storage, so add nothing for it.\n1173\t- **Pause:** the pause menu offers only Resume, Settings and Controls, and the round clock keeps running.\n1174\t\n1175\t**Tests:**\n1176\t- Headless T-HUB-01..08 use a mock `AIHub` in the vm context: connect, ready without input, the card's answers, start\n1177\t  at time 0, progress every second, a single result, time-up, end stopping input and sound, ghost messages at ≤ 20/s\n1178\t  and applied without changing the local score, and `Math.random` not called during the card.\n1179\t- Browser: the real harness in Playwright (§11.7).\n1180\t\n1181\t### 6.22 Attract mode (`35-attract.js`)\n1182\t\n1183\t- **Starts** after **10 s with no input** on the title (its mode menu included) or the other top-level menus (the Tour\n1184\t  menu, Team Select before anyone joins, Derby Setup, the lesson list, About). Input means any key, button, click, touch, stick past the dead zone, or\n1185\t  mouse movement over 4 px.\n1186\t- **Exits** on any input: back to the title (input consumed, so it doesn't pick a menu item); the idle timer restarts.\n1187\t- **What it is:** a looping **highlight reel played by the real game**, run by a director over `game.debug` with\n1188\t  cheats on (forced pitches and contact, infinite meter, no outs).\n1189\t- **On screen:** a \"DEMO PLAY\" banner and a pulsing \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (the icon for the device used last; on\n1190\t  touch-only devices \"TOUCH TO RETURN\"), plus a caption card between segments.\n1191\t- **Segments** (§7.11) cover the Plate Cam duel, super pitches, fielding, a diving catch, a Laser Arm throw, a steal and\n1192\t  slide, a bowl-over, a Batzooka moonshot with fireworks, a Rhubarb, low-gravity wall climbs, the Phantom Ball, the\n1193\t  drones and boss, the Derby with ghost comets, and the Moonshot Leaders table. One loop takes about 2.5 minutes.\n1194\t- **Robustness:** each segment has a time limit and moves on by itself if its event doesn't happen.\n1195\t- **Never** in an AI Hub session.\n1196\t\n1197\t**Tests:** T-ATT-01..05 (idle 10 s on the title starts it; it doesn't start during play or with the dev panel open;\n1198\tevery segment runs in order without errors and the reel loops; any input returns to the title; touch-only mode still\n1199\truns it).\n1200\t\n1201\t### 6.23 Dev mode (`36-dev.js`)\n1202\t\n1203\t**Reached** from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item (any pausable scene; hidden in hub sessions). It is a large,\n1204\t10-foot-readable panel over the frozen game, with six tabs. L1/R1 or Q/E change tabs; up and down move; left and right\n1205\tchange a value (hold to accelerate); ✕ toggles or activates; △ resets this value (or pins a slider); ○ closes. The\n1206\tmouse hovers, clicks, and drags sliders.\n1207\t\n1208\t1. **TUNE**: every `BZ.TUNE` value as a **live slider** grouped as in Appendix A (Pitching, Batting, Ball, Players,\n1209\t   Over the top, CPU, Camera, Game). Values apply instantly.\n1210\t   - **Reset to defaults** for all, and a reset per group.\n1211\t   - \"Keep tuning between visits\" stores the values in `E.store('bz:tune')`.\n1212\t   - **Pinned sliders:** △ pins up to 3. While playing, a thin strip at the top shows them; hold Create (Pad8) with\n1213\t     the D-pad to adjust (keyboard: `[` and `]` adjust, `\\` picks the next pin).\n1214\t2. **SITUATION**: set the inning, half, outs, balls, strikes and score; runners on first, second and third; the\n1215\t   batter; the pitcher's stamina; both meters and turbo; the park; the wind. Then Apply.\n1216\t3. **CHEATS** (toggles):\n1217\t   - Batting and pitching: perfect contact always; every pitch a strike.\n1218\t   - Meters: infinite meter, infinite turbo.\n1219\t   - Play: fielders ignore walls (no clip); the CPU plays my side (autoplay); slow motion ×0.25; freeze the AI.\n1220\t   - Show: the zone always; the predicted pitch path and the timing bar; landing markers and AI targets; catch\n1221\t     radii and hitboxes.\n1222\t4. **TRIGGERS**:\n1223\t   - Force the next pitch (type and spot); force a home run on the next contact.\n1224\t   - Hazard now; meteor shower; Rhubarb; Batzooka cinematic; replay the last play.\n1225\t   - End the half-inning; walk-off now; win the game; lose the game.\n1226\t5. **WARP**:\n1227\t   - Scenes: title, attract, the gallery, the hub card (mocked), credits.\n1228\t   - Play: any Tour stop (pregame, game or postgame), any lesson, the Derby, an Exhibition in any park.\n1229\t   - Save: unlock all, +5,000 FB, reset the save.\n1230\t6. **INFO**:\n1231\t   - Live: fps, scene and phase, the ball's position and velocity, the last contact's numbers (timing ms, offset, Q,\n1232\t     EV, launch, spray), the seed, the input device and glyph family, the last 8 events, `E.versionLabel()`.\n1233\t   - **Frame step** (one 1/120 s step while frozen) and **Copy snapshot** (JSON to the clipboard).\n1234\t\n1235\t**The animation gallery** (from WARP) shows every new animation on rigs in turn, at normal speed or slowed, for review\n1236\twith `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n1237\t\n1238\t**Tests:** T-DEV-01..06 (the pause menu holds Dev Mode; a slider changes `TUNE` and the effect shows in the next pitch;\n1239\treset restores the defaults exactly; the situation applies; cheats toggle; warps land in their scene with no errors).\n1240\t\n1241\t### 6.24 Screens and UX flow (`34-menus.js`)\n1242\t\n1243\t**Principles:**\n1244\t- Big cards, never tables: at most 7 items to a screen.\n1245\t- The focus is obvious: it scales up 10%, gets a bright border and bobs gently.\n1246\t- A legend at the bottom shows glyph icons (\"✕ Select · ○ Back\").\n1247\t- Every screen works with the D-pad/stick, the keyboard (arrows/WASD, Enter/K, Escape/L) and the mouse (hover moves\n1248\t  the focus, click selects). Menus are pixel art drawn with `E.ui.box`, `E.font` and `E.font.title`.\n1249\t\n1250\t**Title:**\n1251\t- The background is the Kernel Field at dusk, seen from the Broadcast Cam, slowly panning, with fireflies; Dot\n1252\t  Dynamite stands with the Batzooka on her shoulder.\n1253\t- The logo \"BATZOOKA BASEBALL\" is drawn with `E.font.title` (scale 4, a gold-orange gradient, depth 3) and a rocket\n1254\t  trail sweeping under it.\n1255\t- Menu: CONTINUE (when there is a save), TOUR, EXHIBITION, DERBY, SPRING TRAINING, OPTIONS, ABOUT.\n1256\t- `E.versionLabel()` in a corner.\n1257\t\n1258\t**Team Select:**\n1259\t- Two big team cards (left away, right home): the captain's rig turning, the team name, three stat stars (Power,\n1260\t  Speed, Pitching), and the park they play in.\n1261\t- Left and right change the team; up and down move between the team, park, innings and difficulty rows.\n1262\t- The join row shows P1–P4 cards that slide to a side.\n1263\t\n1264\t**Results:**\n1265\t- The final score big; a one-line line score (R H E).\n1266\t- The game's **three stars** as cards (portrait, one line each).\n1267\t- FB earned, with a counting-up tween.\n1268\t- Buttons: Continue, Replay highlights, Rematch.\n1269\t\n1270\t**Playbook** (help, from the title's OPTIONS and the pause menu): one page per context (Batting, Pitching, Fielding,\n1271\tRunning, Supers, Rhubarb, House Rules). Each shows a picture of the action in the game's own art (a rig in the pose)\n1272\tand 3–5 big icon + verb lines for the current device.\n1273\t\n1274\t**About/Credits:** §6.27.\n1275\t\n1276\t**Tests:** T-UI-01..06 (every screen reachable and back; mouse hover moves the focus; clicks select; keyboard and pad\n1277\tnavigation; no screen over 7 items; the legend icons match the device).\n1278\t\n1279\t### 6.25 Settings and accessibility\n1280\t\n1281\tOurs are added with `menu: { settings: [...] }` / `settings.define`, beside the engine's own (volume, music, effects,\n1282\treduce motion, shake, flashes, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate, controls, dead zone, vibration):\n1283\t- **Gameplay:** Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / All-Star / Batzooka); Exhibition innings (1/3/5/9); Tour game length\n1284\t  (Standard / Quick); Mercy rule (On/Off); Comeback Boost (On/Off); Rhubarbs (On/Off); Derby length (2:00 / 10 outs).\n1285\t- **Assists:** Batting assist (Off / Timing hints / Big sweet spot); Pitching assist (Off / Auto-aim); Fielding\n1286\t  (Manual / Assisted / Auto); Baserunning (Manual / Auto).\n1287\t- **Display:** Timing feedback (On/Off); Strike zone (Always / During pitch / Off); Plate Cam (Classic / Close);\n1288\t  Field camera (Broadcast / High / Isometric); Replays (On / Big plays / Off).\n1289\t- **Sound:** Commentary (On / Big plays / Off); Voices (a 0–1 slider).\n1290\t- **Controller:** Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox), the engine's setting with our default (§3.3).\n1291\t- **Developer:** \"Keep dev tuning\" (On/Off).\n1292\t\n1293\tReduce motion also softens the camera cuts (fades instead of flashes) and turns off the screen shake in cinematics.\n1294\t\n1295\t### 6.26 Touch-only devices\n1296\t\n1297\t- **Detection, at boot:**\n1298\t  `touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`.\n1299\t  It clears for good when a key is pressed or a gamepad connects (`gamepadconnected`, or `input.padId` set).\n1300\t- **While touch-only:**\n1301\t  - The title shows a large card: a controller and a keyboard icon, \"Controller or keyboard required\", and a big\n1302\t    **Settings** button (it opens `game.menu('settings')`), beside the engine's corner menu button.\n1303\t  - There are no touch controls: `game.input.touchEnabled = false`, no scene has a `touch` list, and the engine's\n1304\t    touch-button settings stay hidden.\n1305\t  - The attract mode runs after 10 s as usual; a tap returns to the title card.\n1306\t  - Tapping menu items does nothing (the menus need a controller or keyboard), except the Settings button and the\n1307\t    corner button.\n1308\t\n1309\t**Tests:** T-TOUCH-01..03 (`#touch` forces the flag: the title shows the card, the menus ignore taps but Settings opens;\n1310\tthe attract mode starts after 10 s; a key press clears the flag).\n1311\t\n1312\t### 6.27 About/Credits, Source Information and the exit interview\n1313\t\n1314\t**The About/Credits screen** (from the title's ABOUT) has pages turned by\n1315\tL1/R1, left/right or clicks. Each page holds at most about 12 lines at scale 1, wrapped to the width.\n1316\t1. **ABOUT:** the logo; \"An original over-the-top arcade baseball game\"; the version (`E.versionLabel()`); the controls\n1317\t   in one line.\n1318\t2. **SOURCE INFORMATION**, every field TASK.md lists, filled in at the end of the build (\"unknown\" for anything that\n1319\t   can't be confirmed):\n1320\t   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:48:19.\n1321\t   - Source: baseball (the sport), in the over-the-top arcade style.\n1322\t   - Plan: `PLAN.md`.\n1323\t   - Genre and Perspective: §2.\n1324\t   - Tech: stack, engine and module versions, the changes made, mocap, the AI Hub client version, and Node and\n1325\t     Playwright for the tests.\n1326\t   - Art Direction, Animation, Audio: as built.\n1327\t   - Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, a ghost-mode Derby round for 1–4 players, client 1.4.0.\n1328\t   - Testing: what was allowed and used.\n1329\t   - Research: what was read.\n1330\t   - Environment: \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\", or what is known.\n1331\t   - Model: as TASK.md gives it.\n1332\t   - Usage: estimates, or \"unknown\".\n1333\t3. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n1334\t4. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the six answers (including what changed in the engine, §3.3).\n1335\t5. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n1336\t6. **CREDITS:**\n1337\t   - Design, code, art, music and writing: the building model, with Batzooka Baseball.\n1338\t   - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT, github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge).\n1339\t   - Motion: the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses); Quaternius and Mesh2Motion (CC0).\n1340\t   - AI Hub Session client 1.4.0 (michaelcrosato/ai-hub).\n1341\t   - Any CC0 asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG).\n1342\t   - \"Thanks for playing!\"\n1343\t\n1344\t**The same text** goes in the builder's final chat reply, and in `exit-interview.json` in exactly TASK.md's shape (§12).\n1345\tIts `aiHub` block should read:\n1346\t- `name`: \"Batzooka Baseball\"; `tagline`: \"Swing for the moon. Literally.\"\n1347\t- `description`: \"Over-the-top arcade baseball: fireball pitches, a rocket-powered bat, wall-climbing catches and\n1348\t  bench-clearing rhubarbs on a barnstorming tour to save a cornfield ballpark.\"\n1349\t- `type`: \"Game\"; `genre`: \"Sports\"; `source`: \"Baseball (over-the-top arcade style)\"; `series`: \"\"; `players`: \"1–4\".\n1350\t- `controls`: \"Stick/WASD/mouse aim · ✕/K/click swing · □/J/right-click power · R1/E Batzooka\".\n1351\t- `tags`: [\"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"boss fights\", \"retro\"].\n1352\t\n1353\t---\n1354\t\n1355\t## 7. Content\n1356\t\n1357\tAll names, teams, parks and lines are original. Stats run 1–10. Batters have POW (power), CON (contact), SPD (speed),\n1358\tARM and GLV (glove); pitchers have VEL (velocity), CTL (control), BRK (break) and STA (stamina). Stat 5 is the ×1.0\n1359\tbaseline, and each point is ±3% on the matching multiplier. B/T is the side they bat / throw from.\n1360\t\n1361\t### 7.1 Teams and rosters (`50-teams.js`)\n1362\t\n1363\t**1. Kernel Falls COMETS** (COM). The heroes: a scrappy farm-town team. Home: Kernel Field.\n1364\t- **Uniform:** cream jerseys and pants `#f4ecd8`, navy trim, cap and belt `#1e2a5a`, gold socks `#f2c230`.\n1365\t- **Mascot:** Popcorn Pete, a cream Blob with butter-yellow spots and feet.\n1366\t- **Team super pitch:** **Corn Popper**: the ball pops three times in flight like a kernel, jittering ±3 U at each pop"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"177ae602-0016-490f-b909-49e6e6a3d747","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:37:31.168Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Session rules:**\n- **No title or restart:** Quit to title, Restart, Dev Mode and Pitching Change are hidden, and the back gesture is\n  swallowed.\n- **No popups or sockets:** no `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, new windows or sockets.\n- **Storage:** the client already gives an empty storage, so add nothing for it.\n- **Pause:** the pause menu offers only Resume, Settings and Controls, and the round clock keeps running.\n\n**Tests:**\n- Headless T-HUB-01..08 use a mock `AIHub` in the vm context: connect, ready without input, the card's answers, start\n  at time 0, progress every second, a single result, time-up, end stopping input and sound, ghost messages at ≤ 20/s\n  and applied without changing the local score, and `Math.random` not called during the card.\n- Browser: the real harness in Playwright (§11.7).\n\n### 6.22 Attract mode (`35-attract.js`)\n\n- **Starts** after **10 s with no input** on the title (its mode menu included) or the other top-level menus (the Tour\n  menu, Team Select before anyone joins, Derby Setup, the lesson list, About). Input means any key, button, click, touch, stick past the dead zone, or\n  mouse movement over 4 px.\n- **Exits** on any input: back to the title (input consumed, so it doesn't pick a menu item); the idle timer restarts.\n- **What it is:** a looping **highlight reel played by the real game**, run by a director over `game.debug` with\n  cheats on (forced pitches and contact, infinite meter, no outs).\n- **On screen:** a \"DEMO PLAY\" banner and a pulsing \"PRESS ANY BUTTON\" (the icon for the device used last; on\n  touch-only devices \"TOUCH TO RETURN\"), plus a caption card between segments.\n- **Segments** (§7.11) cover the Plate Cam duel, super pitches, fielding, a diving catch, a Laser Arm throw, a steal and\n  slide, a bowl-over, a Batzooka moonshot with fireworks, a Rhubarb, low-gravity wall climbs, the Phantom Ball, the\n  drones and boss, the Derby with ghost comets, and the Moonshot Leaders table. One loop takes about 2.5 minutes.\n- **Robustness:** each segment has a time limit and moves on by itself if its event doesn't happen.\n- **Never** in an AI Hub session.\n\n**Tests:** T-ATT-01..05 (idle 10 s on the title starts it; it doesn't start during play or with the dev panel open;\nevery segment runs in order without errors and the reel loops; any input returns to the title; touch-only mode still\nruns it).\n\n### 6.23 Dev mode (`36-dev.js`)\n\n**Reached** from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item (any pausable scene; hidden in hub sessions). It is a large,\n10-foot-readable panel over the frozen game, with six tabs. L1/R1 or Q/E change tabs; up and down move; left and right\nchange a value (hold to accelerate); ✕ toggles or activates; △ resets this value (or pins a slider); ○ closes. The\nmouse hovers, clicks, and drags sliders.\n\n1. **TUNE**: every `BZ.TUNE` value as a **live slider** grouped as in Appendix A (Pitching, Batting, Ball, Players,\n   Over the top, CPU, Camera, Game). Values apply instantly.\n   - **Reset to defaults** for all, and a reset per group.\n   - \"Keep tuning between visits\" stores the values in `E.store('bz:tune')`.\n   - **Pinned sliders:** △ pins up to 3. While playing, a thin strip at the top shows them; hold Create (Pad8) with\n     the D-pad to adjust (keyboard: `[` and `]` adjust, `\\` picks the next pin).\n2. **SITUATION**: set the inning, half, outs, balls, strikes and score; runners on first, second and third; the\n   batter; the pitcher's stamina; both meters and turbo; the park; the wind. Then Apply.\n3. **CHEATS** (toggles):\n   - Batting and pitching: perfect contact always; every pitch a strike.\n   - Meters: infinite meter, infinite turbo.\n   - Play: fielders ignore walls (no clip); the CPU plays my side (autoplay); slow motion ×0.25; freeze the AI.\n   - Show: the zone always; the predicted pitch path and the timing bar; landing markers and AI targets; catch\n     radii and hitboxes.\n4. **TRIGGERS**:\n   - Force the next pitch (type and spot); force a home run on the next contact.\n   - Hazard now; meteor shower; Rhubarb; Batzooka cinematic; replay the last play.\n   - End the half-inning; walk-off now; win the game; lose the game.\n5. **WARP**:\n   - Scenes: title, attract, the gallery, the hub card (mocked), credits.\n   - Play: any Tour stop (pregame, game or postgame), any lesson, the Derby, an Exhibition in any park.\n   - Save: unlock all, +5,000 FB, reset the save.\n6. **INFO**:\n   - Live: fps, scene and phase, the ball's position and velocity, the last contact's numbers (timing ms, offset, Q,\n     EV, launch, spray), the seed, the input device and glyph family, the last 8 events, `E.versionLabel()`.\n   - **Frame step** (one 1/120 s step while frozen) and **Copy snapshot** (JSON to the clipboard).\n\n**The animation gallery** (from WARP) shows every new animation on rigs in turn, at normal speed or slowed, for review\nwith `tools/filmstrip.mjs`.\n\n**Tests:** T-DEV-01..06 (the pause menu holds Dev Mode; a slider changes `TUNE` and the effect shows in the next pitch;\nreset restores the defaults exactly; the situation applies; cheats toggle; warps land in their scene with no errors).\n\n### 6.24 Screens and UX flow (`34-menus.js`)\n\n**Principles:**\n- Big cards, never tables: at most 7 items to a screen.\n- The focus is obvious: it scales up 10%, gets a bright border and bobs gently.\n- A legend at the bottom shows glyph icons (\"✕ Select · ○ Back\").\n- Every screen works with the D-pad/stick, the keyboard (arrows/WASD, Enter/K, Escape/L) and the mouse (hover moves\n  the focus, click selects). Menus are pixel art drawn with `E.ui.box`, `E.font` and `E.font.title`.\n\n**Title:**\n- The background is the Kernel Field at dusk, seen from the Broadcast Cam, slowly panning, with fireflies; Dot\n  Dynamite stands with the Batzooka on her shoulder.\n- The logo \"BATZOOKA BASEBALL\" is drawn with `E.font.title` (scale 4, a gold-orange gradient, depth 3) and a rocket\n  trail sweeping under it.\n- Menu: CONTINUE (when there is a save), TOUR, EXHIBITION, DERBY, SPRING TRAINING, OPTIONS, ABOUT.\n- `E.versionLabel()` in a corner.\n\n**Team Select:**\n- Two big team cards (left away, right home): the captain's rig turning, the team name, three stat stars (Power,\n  Speed, Pitching), and the park they play in.\n- Left and right change the team; up and down move between the team, park, innings and difficulty rows.\n- The join row shows P1–P4 cards that slide to a side.\n\n**Results:**\n- The final score big; a one-line line score (R H E).\n- The game's **three stars** as cards (portrait, one line each).\n- FB earned, with a counting-up tween.\n- Buttons: Continue, Replay highlights, Rematch.\n\n**Playbook** (help, from the title's OPTIONS and the pause menu): one page per context (Batting, Pitching, Fielding,\nRunning, Supers, Rhubarb, House Rules). Each shows a picture of the action in the game's own art (a rig in the pose)\nand 3–5 big icon + verb lines for the current device.\n\n**About/Credits:** §6.27.\n\n**Tests:** T-UI-01..06 (every screen reachable and back; mouse hover moves the focus; clicks select; keyboard and pad\nnavigation; no screen over 7 items; the legend icons match the device).\n\n### 6.25 Settings and accessibility\n\nOurs are added with `menu: { settings: [...] }` / `settings.define`, beside the engine's own (volume, music, effects,\nreduce motion, shake, flashes, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate, controls, dead zone, vibration):\n- **Gameplay:** Difficulty (Rookie / Pro / All-Star / Batzooka); Exhibition innings (1/3/5/9); Tour game length\n  (Standard / Quick); Mercy rule (On/Off); Comeback Boost (On/Off); Rhubarbs (On/Off); Derby length (2:00 / 10 outs).\n- **Assists:** Batting assist (Off / Timing hints / Big sweet spot); Pitching assist (Off / Auto-aim); Fielding\n  (Manual / Assisted / Auto); Baserunning (Manual / Auto).\n- **Display:** Timing feedback (On/Off); Strike zone (Always / During pitch / Off); Plate Cam (Classic / Close);\n  Field camera (Broadcast / High / Isometric); Replays (On / Big plays / Off).\n- **Sound:** Commentary (On / Big plays / Off); Voices (a 0–1 slider).\n- **Controller:** Button symbols (PlayStation / Xbox), the engine's setting with our default (§3.3).\n- **Developer:** \"Keep dev tuning\" (On/Off).\n\nReduce motion also softens the camera cuts (fades instead of flashes) and turns off the screen shake in cinematics.\n\n### 6.26 Touch-only devices\n\n- **Detection, at boot:**\n  `touchOnly = matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)').matches && !matchMedia('(any-pointer: fine)').matches && navigator.maxTouchPoints > 0`.\n  It clears for good when a key is pressed or a gamepad connects (`gamepadconnected`, or `input.padId` set).\n- **While touch-only:**\n  - The title shows a large card: a controller and a keyboard icon, \"Controller or keyboard required\", and a big\n    **Settings** button (it opens `game.menu('settings')`), beside the engine's corner menu button.\n  - There are no touch controls: `game.input.touchEnabled = false`, no scene has a `touch` list, and the engine's\n    touch-button settings stay hidden.\n  - The attract mode runs after 10 s as usual; a tap returns to the title card.\n  - Tapping menu items does nothing (the menus need a controller or keyboard), except the Settings button and the\n    corner button.\n\n**Tests:** T-TOUCH-01..03 (`#touch` forces the flag: the title shows the card, the menus ignore taps but Settings opens;\nthe attract mode starts after 10 s; a key press clears the flag).\n\n### 6.27 About/Credits, Source Information and the exit interview\n\n**The About/Credits screen** (from the title's ABOUT) has pages turned by\nL1/R1, left/right or clicks. Each page holds at most about 12 lines at scale 1, wrapped to the width.\n1. **ABOUT:** the logo; \"An original over-the-top arcade baseball game\"; the version (`E.versionLabel()`); the controls\n   in one line.\n2. **SOURCE INFORMATION**, every field TASK.md lists, filled in at the end of the build (\"unknown\" for anything that\n   can't be confirmed):\n   - Date: 2026-11-03 17:48:19.\n   - Source: baseball (the sport), in the over-the-top arcade style.\n   - Plan: `PLAN.md`.\n   - Genre and Perspective: §2.\n   - Tech: stack, engine and module versions, the changes made, mocap, the AI Hub client version, and Node and\n     Playwright for the tests.\n   - Art Direction, Animation, Audio: as built.\n   - Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, a ghost-mode Derby round for 1–4 players, client 1.4.0.\n   - Testing: what was allowed and used.\n   - Research: what was read.\n   - Environment: \"Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\", or what is known.\n   - Model: as TASK.md gives it.\n   - Usage: estimates, or \"unknown\".\n3. **TESTING FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n4. **ENGINE FEEDBACK:** the six answers (including what changed in the engine, §3.3).\n5. **PROMPT FEEDBACK:** the four answers.\n6. **CREDITS:**\n   - Design, code, art, music and writing: the building model, with Batzooka Baseball.\n   - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT, github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge).\n   - Motion: the CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses); Quaternius and Mesh2Motion (CC0).\n   - AI Hub Session client 1.4.0 (michaelcrosato/ai-hub).\n   - Any CC0 asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit, ambientCG).\n   - \"Thanks for playing!\"\n\n**The same text** goes in the builder's final chat reply, and in `exit-interview.json` in exactly TASK.md's shape (§12).\nIts `aiHub` block should read:\n- `name`: \"Batzooka Baseball\"; `tagline`: \"Swing for the moon. Literally.\"\n- `description`: \"Over-the-top arcade baseball: fireball pitches, a rocket-powered bat, wall-climbing catches and\n  bench-clearing rhubarbs on a barnstorming tour to save a cornfield ballpark.\"\n- `type`: \"Game\"; `genre`: \"Sports\"; `source`: \"Baseball (over-the-top arcade style)\"; `series`: \"\"; `players`: \"1–4\".\n- `controls`: \"Stick/WASD/mouse aim · ✕/K/click swing · □/J/right-click power · R1/E Batzooka\".\n- `tags`: [\"arcade\", \"comedy\", \"versus\", \"pixel art\", \"boss fights\", \"retro\"].\n\n---\n\n## 7. Content\n\nAll names, teams, parks and lines are original. Stats run 1–10. Batters have POW (power), CON (contact), SPD (speed),\nARM and GLV (glove); pitchers have VEL (velocity), CTL (control), BRK (break) and STA (stamina). Stat 5 is the ×1.0\nbaseline, and each point is ±3% on the matching multiplier. B/T is the side they bat / throw from.\n\n### 7.1 Teams and rosters (`50-teams.js`)\n\n**1. Kernel Falls COMETS** (COM). The heroes: a scrappy farm-town team. Home: Kernel Field.\n- **Uniform:** cream jerseys and pants `#f4ecd8`, navy trim, cap and belt `#1e2a5a`, gold socks `#f2c230`.\n- **Mascot:** Popcorn Pete, a cream Blob with butter-yellow spots and feet.\n- **Team super pitch:** **Corn Popper**: the ball pops three times in flight like a kernel, jittering ±3 U at each pop","numLines":200,"startLine":1167,"totalLines":2120}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PpshpLfYNkeG3AYb6zfv4W","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
