{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014MNsZYidJcZLbRd64pmBu4","type":"tool_result","content":"1356\t\n1357\tAll names, teams, parks and lines are original. Stats run 1–10. Batters have POW (power), CON (contact), SPD (speed),\n1358\tARM and GLV (glove); pitchers have VEL (velocity), CTL (control), BRK (break) and STA (stamina). Stat 5 is the ×1.0\n1359\tbaseline: a stat's factor is `1 + 0.03 · (stat − 5)` (0.88–1.15), unless a formula says otherwise. B/T is the side they bat / throw from.\n1360\t\n1361\t### 7.1 Teams and rosters (`50-teams.js`)\n1362\t\n1363\t**1. Kernel Falls COMETS** (COM). The heroes: a scrappy farm-town team. Home: Kernel Field.\n1364\t- **Uniform:** cream jerseys and pants `#f4ecd8`, navy trim, cap and belt `#1e2a5a`, gold socks `#f2c230`.\n1365\t- **Mascot:** Popcorn Pete, a cream Blob with butter-yellow spots and feet.\n1366\t- **Team super pitch:** **Corn Popper**: the ball pops three times in flight like a kernel, jittering ±3 U at each pop\n1367\t  with a \"pok!\" sound.\n1368\t- **Lineup:**\n1369\t\n1370\t| Pos | Name | B/T | POW CON SPD ARM GLV (pitchers: VEL CTL BRK STA) | Look and notes |\n1371\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1372\t| CF | **Dot \"Dynamite\" Delgado** (captain) | R/R | 9 8 7 7 7 | heroic build, ponytail, warm brown skin; wields the Batzooka; voice pulse12 300 Hz |\n1373\t| SS | Pep Porter | L/R | 4 8 9 7 9 | twin; chibi build, freckles |\n1374\t| 2B | Pip Porter | R/R | 4 7 9 6 8 | Pep's twin, mirror palette |\n1375\t| 1B | Moose Magnusson | L/L | 9 5 3 5 6 | bulky, blond braid |\n1376\t| 3B | Sunny Sato | R/R | 6 7 6 8 8 | always smiling (`expr: 'smile'`) |\n1377\t| C | Rosa \"Radar\" Reyes | R/R | 6 6 4 9 8 | mask, catcher's mitt |\n1378\t| LF | Lefty Luna | L/L | 5 8 8 6 7 | slap hitter |\n1379\t| RF | Hank \"Hambone\" Hollis | R/R | 8 5 5 9 6 | bulky; eats between pitches |\n1380\t| P | **Grandpa Ike Kowalski** | R/R | 4 8 9 6 | hunch .3, bald, white sides; signature **Butterfly Knuckler**; voice triangle 170 Hz, shaky; the coach |\n1381\t| RP | Kid Kernel | R/R | 9 5 5 4 | teenager; all heat |\n1382\t\n1383\t**2. Harbor City KRAKENS** (HCK). Home: Barnacle Bay Park.\n1384\t- **Uniform:** teal `#1f8a8a`, coral trim `#ff7a5c`, sand pants `#e8d8b0`, sailor-stripe socks.\n1385\t- **Mascot:** Squidge, a purple Blob with a big mouth.\n1386\t- **Captain and ace:** **Captain Bettina Brine** (P, R/L, 7 7 8 7). Signature **Riptide Curve** (a curve that dips,\n1387\t  rises and dips: a sine of amplitude 4 U along its path). Team super **Tidal Wave** (the ball rides a translucent wave\n1388\t  sprite that rises 10 U and crashes down through the zone). Voice: pulse at 200 Hz.\n1389\t- **Lineup:** C \"Barnacle\" Barney Finn · 1B Coral Quinn · 2B Skip Marlin · SS Wade Waters · 3B Gil Gruber ·\n1390\t  LF Shelly Shoals · CF Dash Seaborne · RF Hook Hardy · RP Rip Tidewell.\n1391\t\n1392\t**3. Magma City ERUPTORS** (MCE). Home: Caldera Field.\n1393\t- **Uniform:** charcoal `#2b2b30`, lava orange `#ff6a1a` with yellow trim; caps with flame bills.\n1394\t- **Mascot:** Sparky, a glowing orange Blob that drips embers.\n1395\t- **Captain and ace:** **Iggy \"The Igniter\" Blaze** (P, R/R, 9 6 7 7). Signature **Magma Sinker** (a late drop of\n1396\t  −10 U with an ember trail). Team super **Meteor Heater** (a fireball at 1.35× speed with a flame trail and heat\n1397\t  shimmer; the catcher's mitt smokes). Voice: square at 230 Hz, fast. He is a hothead, and he starts the Tour's\n1398\t  scripted Rhubarb.\n1399\t- **Lineup:** C Basalt Bruno · 1B Magnus Holt · 2B Cinder Ellis · SS Ashley Pyre · 3B \"Hot Corner\" Hector Flores ·\n1400\t  LF Ember Okafor · CF Flint Rocha · RF Sol Vulcan · RP Scorch McGee.\n1401\t\n1402\t**4. Moonbase METEORS** (MBM). Home: Tranquility Dome.\n1403\t- **Uniform:** silver `#c8d0e0`, cosmic purple `#6a4cff`, white; `hat: 'visor'` space helmets in the field.\n1404\t- **Mascot:** Moonpie, a grey cratered Blob that floats.\n1405\t- **Captain and ace:** **Commander Cosmo Vega** (P, L/L, 6 8 9 8). Signature **Zero-G Floater** (slow, 0.62×; it\n1406\t  rises 6 U and then drops 12 U late). Team super **Black Hole Ball** (the ball shrinks to a dot with a dark swirl,\n1407\t  and a batter's reticle within 10 U is pulled 3 U toward it). Voice: sine at 210 Hz with vibrato.\n1408\t- **Lineup:** C Orbit Okoye · 1B Nova Nakamura · 2B Stella Petrov · SS Quasar Diaz · 3B Rocket Rhodes ·\n1409\t  LF Astra Bell · CF Halley Brooks · RF Gus Gravitas · RP Pulsar Penn.\n1410\t\n1411\t**5. Hollowmoor HAUNTS** (HMH). Home: Boneyard Ballpark. Players are `build: 'skeleton'` with `colors.bone`.\n1412\t- **Uniform:** bone `#e8e0c8`, midnight `#1a1630`, ghost green `#7dffb0`; tattered caps.\n1413\t- **Mascot:** Boo, a white Blob with a front face, drawn translucent.\n1414\t- **Captain and ace:** **Count Rattlebones** (P, R/R, 7 8 9 9). Signature **Phantom Forkball** (invisible for\n1415\t  u 0.35–0.8, then a sharp −8 U drop). Team super **Banshee Ball** (invisible until u 0.85, with a scream sound and\n1416\t  a screen flicker). Voice: triangle at 220 Hz with clacks.\n1417\t- **Lineup:** C Mort Graves · 1B Boney Malone · 2B Wailin' Winnie · SS Skelly Kelly · 3B Ezekiel Tomb · LF Shade Murphy ·\n1418\t  CF Wisp O'Hara · RF Digger Doyle · RP Spook Hennessy.\n1419\t\n1420\t**6. MegaMax MECHANICALS** (MMX). The boss team. Home: the MegaMax MegaDome. Players are robot Humanoids: metal\n1421\tcolors, `eyeGlow`, helmets, and `build: 'bulky'` for some.\n1422\t- **Uniform:** chrome `#b8c0cc`, corporate red `#e01e3c`, neon cyan `#2de2e6`.\n1423\t- **Mascot:** Mr. Synergy, a chrome Blob with wings: a hovering drone with a smiley screen.\n1424\t- **Ace and boss:** **ENFORCER-9000** (P, R/R, 10 8 6 10, `size: 2.2`, bulky, red eye glow). Signature **Gigavolt\n1425\t  Heater** (1.25× with an electric zig-zag of ±2 U). Team super **Overclock Laser** (1.5×, perfectly straight, with a\n1426\t  laser trail; only hittable with a GOOD timing or better).\n1427\t- **Boss rules:**\n1428\t  - **Overclock:** his pitch speed rises 5% each inning.\n1429\t  - **Short circuit:** a home run off him short-circuits him for the next half-inning: speed ×0.85, sparks, a\n1430\t    stutter in his windup.\n1431\t  - **Rally Cap:** if the Comets trail entering their last turn at bat, the stands (full of the beaten rival teams)\n1432\t    start the Rally Cap chant and the Comets' meter fills.\n1433\t- **Lineup:** C Backstop-X · 1B Forklift · 2B Servo · SS Sprocket · 3B Torque · LF Router · CF Byte · RF Piston ·\n1434\t  RP Spare Part.\n1435\t\n1436\t**Non-players:**\n1437\t- **Mortimer Megamax:** the villain, owner of MegaMax Corp. `outfit: 'coat'`, `hat: 'tophat'` (§3.3), a gold watch chain; voice saw at 140 Hz. He watches from a luxury box in the MegaDome.\n1438\t- **HAP HARRIGAN:** headset band, sweater vest.\n1439\t- **BIG LOU BOMBECK:** bulky, bald, a 1979 championship ring.\n1440\t- **GLORIA VOX:** the PA, a portrait only.\n1441\t- **UMPIRE BARB HAMMERSMITH:** navy coat, cap and mask.\n1442\t- **Grounds crew, vendors, fans:** generic rigs and the crowd.\n1443\t\n1444\t### 7.2 Parks (`51-parks.js`)\n1445\t\n1446\t| Park | Team | Time and sky | Fence LF / LC / CF / RC / RF (U), height | Ground beyond | Lights | Weather | Music |\n1447\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n1448\t| **Kernel Field** | Comets | golden late afternoon: a custom Backdrop with hills, farmland, a windmill, clouds, a low sun | 980 / 1080 / 1180 / 1060 / 950, h 40 | cornfield (rows of `cornstalk` shapes), the silo in right, a red-barn scoreboard | ambient 0.85, warm sun tint; string lights come on in the evening | light leaves | county-fair organ |\n1449\t| **Barnacle Bay Park** | Krakens | bright noon: the `ocean` preset plus gulls | 1000 / 1100 / 1150 / 1000 / 900 (RF h 30), others h 40 | the bay beyond right (a `water` floor with bobbing boats), a pier, a lighthouse in left | lights off (day) | wind out to left | 6/8 shanty |\n1450\t| **Caldera Field** | Eruptors | dusk: a dark red sky, the volcano, a smoke plume | 920 / 1060 / 1200 / 1100 / 1000, h 50 (basalt) | a lava moat (a `lava` floor, glowing `[r, g, b, glow]`), basalt columns | ambient 0.55; orange lava lights along the fence; 4 light towers | ash | minor drums, saw bass |\n1451\t| **Tranquility Dome** | Meteors | lunar night: the `space` preset, a big Earth disc, the dome's ribs drawn as arcs | 1350 / 1450 / 1550 / 1450 / 1350, h 60 | regolith with craters, habitat modules, antennas, a rover | ambient 0.55; cold blue-white floods | none (\"no air, no wind, no excuses\") | spacey arpeggios |\n1452\t| **Boneyard Ballpark** | Haunts | midnight: a full moon and fog layers | 1000 / 1080 / 1120 / 1080 / 1000, h 36 (an iron cemetery fence) | tombstones, crypts, dead trees, lanterns, candles | ambient 0.45; green and blue lanterns; jack-o'-lantern glow | leaves, fog | spooky organ, theremin |\n1453\t| **MegaMax MegaDome** | Mechanicals | neon night: the `city-night` preset seen through the dome's glass ribs, holo-billboards | 1000 / 1060 / 1100 / 1060 / 1000, h 40; the **Mega Wall** in left (θ −45° to −20°) is h 90 | a neon concourse floor (cyan grid lines), the luxury box, drones | ambient 0.6; magenta and cyan neon lights; the MEGA-TRON's glow | none (indoors) | synthwave |\n1454\t\n1455\t**Per-park physics** (in the park def): `gravityMul` (moon 0.55), `evMul` (moon 0.8), `jumpMul` (moon 2.0), `bounceMul`\n1456\t(dome turf 1.1), and the outfielders' depth shift (moon +200 U). **Floor materials:** grass with the park's mow pattern\n1457\t(Kernel stripes, Barnacle checkerboard, Caldera dark burnt grass, Tranquility bright astroturf, Boneyard dead brown-green,\n1458\tMegaDome turf with cyan neon lines).\n1459\t\n1460\t### 7.3 Pitch catalog (`11-pitch.js` data)\n1461\t\n1462\tThe heater's base speed is 340 U/s. Break is in U at the plate (+x is toward the glove side for a right-handed\n1463\tpitcher); k is the lateness exponent.\n1464\t\n1465\t| Pitch | Speed × | Break x, z | k | Special |\n1466\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1467\t| Heater (fastball) | 1.00 | 0, +1.5 | 1.0 | a little \"rise\" |\n1468\t| Curve (\"Uncle Charlie\") | 0.74 | +7, −10 | 2.2 | |\n1469\t| Slider | 0.86 | +9, −3 | 2.0 | |\n1470\t| Changeup (\"the Pillow\") | 0.66 | −3, −6 | 1.6 | |\n1471\t| Sinker | 0.92 | −4, −6 | 1.8 | |\n1472\t| Knuckler | 0.60 | 0, −3 | – | wobble: noise of amplitude 4 at 3 Hz from the pitch's own seed |\n1473\t| *Signatures* | | | | Butterfly Knuckler (knuckler ×1.6 wobble, it flutters), Riptide Curve, Magma Sinker, Zero-G Floater, Phantom Forkball, Gigavolt Heater (§7.1) |\n1474\t| *Team supers* | ×1.35 unless stated | | | Corn Popper, Tidal Wave, Meteor Heater, Black Hole Ball, Banshee Ball, Overclock Laser (§7.1) |\n1475\t| Pitch-O-Matic (Derby) | 0.80 | small random breaks from `rng.deal` | – | 80% in the zone; every 5th is a Golden Ball |\n1476\t\n1477\tRepertoires: Ike (heater, curve, knuckler, Butterfly); Kid Kernel (heater, slider, changeup, signature = a 1.15×\n1478\t\"Kernel Cannon\" heater); each rival ace (heater, curve or slider, changeup or sinker, signature); relievers (heater,\n1479\tslider, changeup, the team's signature).\n1480\t\n1481\t### 7.4 Supers\n1482\t\n1483\tThe supers are specified in §6.7; each team's super pitch is in §7.1. **Everyone shares** the Batzooka swing (the\n1484\tComets' bat is \"the original\"; rivals have knock-offs drawn in their team colors: the \"Krakenzooka\", \"Lavazooka\",\n1485\t\"Lunazooka\", \"Ghoulzooka\" and \"MEGAZOOKA 9000\"), Laser Arm and Afterburners.\n1486\t\n1487\t### 7.5 The Tour: story and cutscenes (`52-story.js`)\n1488\t\n1489\t**The story.** Kernel Field, home of the Comets since forever, is about to become a parking lot. Mortimer Megamax bets\n1490\tthe deed on the Kaboom Cup, a barnstorming tour of the wildest parks in baseball. The Comets' secret weapon is\n1491\tGrandma Delgado's homemade Batzooka, which only fires when the crowd roars. Each stop is a cutscene (in the Broadcast\n1492\tCam, with rigs, poses and dialog portraits), then the game (with scripted radio lines when its hazard first shows),\n1493\tthen a post-game scene.\n1494\t\n1495\t**Prologue: \"Last Game at Kernel Field?\"** (Kernel Field at dusk, after a practice)\n1496\t- HAP: \"Good evening, baseball fans, from Kernel Field, where the corn is high and the stakes are higher!\"\n1497\t- *A limousine rolls up the foul line. A bulldozer follows it.*\n1498\t- MORTIMER: \"Enjoy your little cornfield, Comets. Monday it's a parking lot. Premium spaces only.\"\n1499\t- DOT: \"Over my dead batting glove.\"\n1500\t- MORTIMER: \"Win the Kaboom Cup and I'll tear up the deed. Lose, and I pave the park AND hang that bat in my lobby.\"\n1501\t- IKE: *(opens a dusty crate)* \"Your grandma's BATZOOKA. Hickory, duct tape and a surplus bottle rocket. Summer of '62.\"\n1502\t- DOT: \"What does it do?\"\n1503\t- IKE: \"Nothin'. Till the crowd gets loud. Then it does EVERYTHING.\"\n1504\t- LOU: \"Folks, I haven't seen a bat that dangerous since I swung at my own shadow in '79!\"\n1505\t- → Offer Spring Training (\"Learn the ropes with Grandpa Ike?\" PLAY · SKIP), then the Tour Map."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"9866f3af-8f92-4481-81c9-83b68d2ae714","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:38:10.975Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work/PLAN.md","content":"\nAll names, teams, parks and lines are original. Stats run 1–10. Batters have POW (power), CON (contact), SPD (speed),\nARM and GLV (glove); pitchers have VEL (velocity), CTL (control), BRK (break) and STA (stamina). Stat 5 is the ×1.0\nbaseline: a stat's factor is `1 + 0.03 · (stat − 5)` (0.88–1.15), unless a formula says otherwise. B/T is the side they bat / throw from.\n\n### 7.1 Teams and rosters (`50-teams.js`)\n\n**1. Kernel Falls COMETS** (COM). The heroes: a scrappy farm-town team. Home: Kernel Field.\n- **Uniform:** cream jerseys and pants `#f4ecd8`, navy trim, cap and belt `#1e2a5a`, gold socks `#f2c230`.\n- **Mascot:** Popcorn Pete, a cream Blob with butter-yellow spots and feet.\n- **Team super pitch:** **Corn Popper**: the ball pops three times in flight like a kernel, jittering ±3 U at each pop\n  with a \"pok!\" sound.\n- **Lineup:**\n\n| Pos | Name | B/T | POW CON SPD ARM GLV (pitchers: VEL CTL BRK STA) | Look and notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CF | **Dot \"Dynamite\" Delgado** (captain) | R/R | 9 8 7 7 7 | heroic build, ponytail, warm brown skin; wields the Batzooka; voice pulse12 300 Hz |\n| SS | Pep Porter | L/R | 4 8 9 7 9 | twin; chibi build, freckles |\n| 2B | Pip Porter | R/R | 4 7 9 6 8 | Pep's twin, mirror palette |\n| 1B | Moose Magnusson | L/L | 9 5 3 5 6 | bulky, blond braid |\n| 3B | Sunny Sato | R/R | 6 7 6 8 8 | always smiling (`expr: 'smile'`) |\n| C | Rosa \"Radar\" Reyes | R/R | 6 6 4 9 8 | mask, catcher's mitt |\n| LF | Lefty Luna | L/L | 5 8 8 6 7 | slap hitter |\n| RF | Hank \"Hambone\" Hollis | R/R | 8 5 5 9 6 | bulky; eats between pitches |\n| P | **Grandpa Ike Kowalski** | R/R | 4 8 9 6 | hunch .3, bald, white sides; signature **Butterfly Knuckler**; voice triangle 170 Hz, shaky; the coach |\n| RP | Kid Kernel | R/R | 9 5 5 4 | teenager; all heat |\n\n**2. Harbor City KRAKENS** (HCK). Home: Barnacle Bay Park.\n- **Uniform:** teal `#1f8a8a`, coral trim `#ff7a5c`, sand pants `#e8d8b0`, sailor-stripe socks.\n- **Mascot:** Squidge, a purple Blob with a big mouth.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Captain Bettina Brine** (P, R/L, 7 7 8 7). Signature **Riptide Curve** (a curve that dips,\n  rises and dips: a sine of amplitude 4 U along its path). Team super **Tidal Wave** (the ball rides a translucent wave\n  sprite that rises 10 U and crashes down through the zone). Voice: pulse at 200 Hz.\n- **Lineup:** C \"Barnacle\" Barney Finn · 1B Coral Quinn · 2B Skip Marlin · SS Wade Waters · 3B Gil Gruber ·\n  LF Shelly Shoals · CF Dash Seaborne · RF Hook Hardy · RP Rip Tidewell.\n\n**3. Magma City ERUPTORS** (MCE). Home: Caldera Field.\n- **Uniform:** charcoal `#2b2b30`, lava orange `#ff6a1a` with yellow trim; caps with flame bills.\n- **Mascot:** Sparky, a glowing orange Blob that drips embers.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Iggy \"The Igniter\" Blaze** (P, R/R, 9 6 7 7). Signature **Magma Sinker** (a late drop of\n  −10 U with an ember trail). Team super **Meteor Heater** (a fireball at 1.35× speed with a flame trail and heat\n  shimmer; the catcher's mitt smokes). Voice: square at 230 Hz, fast. He is a hothead, and he starts the Tour's\n  scripted Rhubarb.\n- **Lineup:** C Basalt Bruno · 1B Magnus Holt · 2B Cinder Ellis · SS Ashley Pyre · 3B \"Hot Corner\" Hector Flores ·\n  LF Ember Okafor · CF Flint Rocha · RF Sol Vulcan · RP Scorch McGee.\n\n**4. Moonbase METEORS** (MBM). Home: Tranquility Dome.\n- **Uniform:** silver `#c8d0e0`, cosmic purple `#6a4cff`, white; `hat: 'visor'` space helmets in the field.\n- **Mascot:** Moonpie, a grey cratered Blob that floats.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Commander Cosmo Vega** (P, L/L, 6 8 9 8). Signature **Zero-G Floater** (slow, 0.62×; it\n  rises 6 U and then drops 12 U late). Team super **Black Hole Ball** (the ball shrinks to a dot with a dark swirl,\n  and a batter's reticle within 10 U is pulled 3 U toward it). Voice: sine at 210 Hz with vibrato.\n- **Lineup:** C Orbit Okoye · 1B Nova Nakamura · 2B Stella Petrov · SS Quasar Diaz · 3B Rocket Rhodes ·\n  LF Astra Bell · CF Halley Brooks · RF Gus Gravitas · RP Pulsar Penn.\n\n**5. Hollowmoor HAUNTS** (HMH). Home: Boneyard Ballpark. Players are `build: 'skeleton'` with `colors.bone`.\n- **Uniform:** bone `#e8e0c8`, midnight `#1a1630`, ghost green `#7dffb0`; tattered caps.\n- **Mascot:** Boo, a white Blob with a front face, drawn translucent.\n- **Captain and ace:** **Count Rattlebones** (P, R/R, 7 8 9 9). Signature **Phantom Forkball** (invisible for\n  u 0.35–0.8, then a sharp −8 U drop). Team super **Banshee Ball** (invisible until u 0.85, with a scream sound and\n  a screen flicker). Voice: triangle at 220 Hz with clacks.\n- **Lineup:** C Mort Graves · 1B Boney Malone · 2B Wailin' Winnie · SS Skelly Kelly · 3B Ezekiel Tomb · LF Shade Murphy ·\n  CF Wisp O'Hara · RF Digger Doyle · RP Spook Hennessy.\n\n**6. MegaMax MECHANICALS** (MMX). The boss team. Home: the MegaMax MegaDome. Players are robot Humanoids: metal\ncolors, `eyeGlow`, helmets, and `build: 'bulky'` for some.\n- **Uniform:** chrome `#b8c0cc`, corporate red `#e01e3c`, neon cyan `#2de2e6`.\n- **Mascot:** Mr. Synergy, a chrome Blob with wings: a hovering drone with a smiley screen.\n- **Ace and boss:** **ENFORCER-9000** (P, R/R, 10 8 6 10, `size: 2.2`, bulky, red eye glow). Signature **Gigavolt\n  Heater** (1.25× with an electric zig-zag of ±2 U). Team super **Overclock Laser** (1.5×, perfectly straight, with a\n  laser trail; only hittable with a GOOD timing or better).\n- **Boss rules:**\n  - **Overclock:** his pitch speed rises 5% each inning.\n  - **Short circuit:** a home run off him short-circuits him for the next half-inning: speed ×0.85, sparks, a\n    stutter in his windup.\n  - **Rally Cap:** if the Comets trail entering their last turn at bat, the stands (full of the beaten rival teams)\n    start the Rally Cap chant and the Comets' meter fills.\n- **Lineup:** C Backstop-X · 1B Forklift · 2B Servo · SS Sprocket · 3B Torque · LF Router · CF Byte · RF Piston ·\n  RP Spare Part.\n\n**Non-players:**\n- **Mortimer Megamax:** the villain, owner of MegaMax Corp. `outfit: 'coat'`, `hat: 'tophat'` (§3.3), a gold watch chain; voice saw at 140 Hz. He watches from a luxury box in the MegaDome.\n- **HAP HARRIGAN:** headset band, sweater vest.\n- **BIG LOU BOMBECK:** bulky, bald, a 1979 championship ring.\n- **GLORIA VOX:** the PA, a portrait only.\n- **UMPIRE BARB HAMMERSMITH:** navy coat, cap and mask.\n- **Grounds crew, vendors, fans:** generic rigs and the crowd.\n\n### 7.2 Parks (`51-parks.js`)\n\n| Park | Team | Time and sky | Fence LF / LC / CF / RC / RF (U), height | Ground beyond | Lights | Weather | Music |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **Kernel Field** | Comets | golden late afternoon: a custom Backdrop with hills, farmland, a windmill, clouds, a low sun | 980 / 1080 / 1180 / 1060 / 950, h 40 | cornfield (rows of `cornstalk` shapes), the silo in right, a red-barn scoreboard | ambient 0.85, warm sun tint; string lights come on in the evening | light leaves | county-fair organ |\n| **Barnacle Bay Park** | Krakens | bright noon: the `ocean` preset plus gulls | 1000 / 1100 / 1150 / 1000 / 900 (RF h 30), others h 40 | the bay beyond right (a `water` floor with bobbing boats), a pier, a lighthouse in left | lights off (day) | wind out to left | 6/8 shanty |\n| **Caldera Field** | Eruptors | dusk: a dark red sky, the volcano, a smoke plume | 920 / 1060 / 1200 / 1100 / 1000, h 50 (basalt) | a lava moat (a `lava` floor, glowing `[r, g, b, glow]`), basalt columns | ambient 0.55; orange lava lights along the fence; 4 light towers | ash | minor drums, saw bass |\n| **Tranquility Dome** | Meteors | lunar night: the `space` preset, a big Earth disc, the dome's ribs drawn as arcs | 1350 / 1450 / 1550 / 1450 / 1350, h 60 | regolith with craters, habitat modules, antennas, a rover | ambient 0.55; cold blue-white floods | none (\"no air, no wind, no excuses\") | spacey arpeggios |\n| **Boneyard Ballpark** | Haunts | midnight: a full moon and fog layers | 1000 / 1080 / 1120 / 1080 / 1000, h 36 (an iron cemetery fence) | tombstones, crypts, dead trees, lanterns, candles | ambient 0.45; green and blue lanterns; jack-o'-lantern glow | leaves, fog | spooky organ, theremin |\n| **MegaMax MegaDome** | Mechanicals | neon night: the `city-night` preset seen through the dome's glass ribs, holo-billboards | 1000 / 1060 / 1100 / 1060 / 1000, h 40; the **Mega Wall** in left (θ −45° to −20°) is h 90 | a neon concourse floor (cyan grid lines), the luxury box, drones | ambient 0.6; magenta and cyan neon lights; the MEGA-TRON's glow | none (indoors) | synthwave |\n\n**Per-park physics** (in the park def): `gravityMul` (moon 0.55), `evMul` (moon 0.8), `jumpMul` (moon 2.0), `bounceMul`\n(dome turf 1.1), and the outfielders' depth shift (moon +200 U). **Floor materials:** grass with the park's mow pattern\n(Kernel stripes, Barnacle checkerboard, Caldera dark burnt grass, Tranquility bright astroturf, Boneyard dead brown-green,\nMegaDome turf with cyan neon lines).\n\n### 7.3 Pitch catalog (`11-pitch.js` data)\n\nThe heater's base speed is 340 U/s. Break is in U at the plate (+x is toward the glove side for a right-handed\npitcher); k is the lateness exponent.\n\n| Pitch | Speed × | Break x, z | k | Special |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Heater (fastball) | 1.00 | 0, +1.5 | 1.0 | a little \"rise\" |\n| Curve (\"Uncle Charlie\") | 0.74 | +7, −10 | 2.2 | |\n| Slider | 0.86 | +9, −3 | 2.0 | |\n| Changeup (\"the Pillow\") | 0.66 | −3, −6 | 1.6 | |\n| Sinker | 0.92 | −4, −6 | 1.8 | |\n| Knuckler | 0.60 | 0, −3 | – | wobble: noise of amplitude 4 at 3 Hz from the pitch's own seed |\n| *Signatures* | | | | Butterfly Knuckler (knuckler ×1.6 wobble, it flutters), Riptide Curve, Magma Sinker, Zero-G Floater, Phantom Forkball, Gigavolt Heater (§7.1) |\n| *Team supers* | ×1.35 unless stated | | | Corn Popper, Tidal Wave, Meteor Heater, Black Hole Ball, Banshee Ball, Overclock Laser (§7.1) |\n| Pitch-O-Matic (Derby) | 0.80 | small random breaks from `rng.deal` | – | 80% in the zone; every 5th is a Golden Ball |\n\nRepertoires: Ike (heater, curve, knuckler, Butterfly); Kid Kernel (heater, slider, changeup, signature = a 1.15×\n\"Kernel Cannon\" heater); each rival ace (heater, curve or slider, changeup or sinker, signature); relievers (heater,\nslider, changeup, the team's signature).\n\n### 7.4 Supers\n\nThe supers are specified in §6.7; each team's super pitch is in §7.1. **Everyone shares** the Batzooka swing (the\nComets' bat is \"the original\"; rivals have knock-offs drawn in their team colors: the \"Krakenzooka\", \"Lavazooka\",\n\"Lunazooka\", \"Ghoulzooka\" and \"MEGAZOOKA 9000\"), Laser Arm and Afterburners.\n\n### 7.5 The Tour: story and cutscenes (`52-story.js`)\n\n**The story.** Kernel Field, home of the Comets since forever, is about to become a parking lot. Mortimer Megamax bets\nthe deed on the Kaboom Cup, a barnstorming tour of the wildest parks in baseball. The Comets' secret weapon is\nGrandma Delgado's homemade Batzooka, which only fires when the crowd roars. Each stop is a cutscene (in the Broadcast\nCam, with rigs, poses and dialog portraits), then the game (with scripted radio lines when its hazard first shows),\nthen a post-game scene.\n\n**Prologue: \"Last Game at Kernel Field?\"** (Kernel Field at dusk, after a practice)\n- HAP: \"Good evening, baseball fans, from Kernel Field, where the corn is high and the stakes are higher!\"\n- *A limousine rolls up the foul line. A bulldozer follows it.*\n- MORTIMER: \"Enjoy your little cornfield, Comets. Monday it's a parking lot. Premium spaces only.\"\n- DOT: \"Over my dead batting glove.\"\n- MORTIMER: \"Win the Kaboom Cup and I'll tear up the deed. Lose, and I pave the park AND hang that bat in my lobby.\"\n- IKE: *(opens a dusty crate)* \"Your grandma's BATZOOKA. Hickory, duct tape and a surplus bottle rocket. Summer of '62.\"\n- DOT: \"What does it do?\"\n- IKE: \"Nothin'. Till the crowd gets loud. Then it does EVERYTHING.\"\n- LOU: \"Folks, I haven't seen a bat that dangerous since I swung at my own shadow in '79!\"\n- → Offer Spring Training (\"Learn the ropes with Grandpa Ike?\" PLAY · SKIP), then the Tour Map.","numLines":150,"startLine":1356,"totalLines":2120}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_014MNsZYidJcZLbRd64pmBu4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
