{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F3ed9Y6rpVLVc5cUutLRFd","type":"tool_result","content":"1508\t- → Offer Spring Training (\"Learn the ropes with Grandpa Ike?\" PLAY · SKIP), then the Tour Map.\n1509\t\n1510\t**Stop 1: Barnacle Bay Park vs the Krakens.**\n1511\t- *Pregame:* BRINE: \"Ahoy, corn-pickers! The tide's coming in, and it's bringing a whole ocean of hurt!\" DOT: \"We\n1512\t  brought sunscreen.\" LOU: \"Watch the gulls, folks. They've got better hands than my old infield.\"\n1513\t- *First gull snatch:* HAP: \"A seagull just stole a fly ball! Is that legal? Barb says it's... in play!\"\n1514\t- *Win:* BRINE: \"Blast it all. Take this. Barnacle Grip Tape. Sticks to anything, except a lead.\" (Lumber +1.)\n1515\t- *Loss:* BRINE: \"Back to the shallow end, landlubbers!\"\n1516\t\n1517\t**Stop 2: Caldera Field vs the Eruptors.**\n1518\t- *Pregame:* IGGY: \"Hope you packed sunscreen. SPF one million.\" IKE: \"Don't stand on anything that's glowing.\"\n1519\t- *First vent:* HAP: \"The ground just sneezed lava, and the baseball went with it!\"\n1520\t- *Scripted Rhubarb* (the first time Iggy hits a batter, or in the 2nd inning by script): LOU: \"Uh-oh, the benches\n1521\t  are emptying! Somebody fetch a fire extinguisher and a referee!\" BARB (after): \"Everybody back in your dugouts\n1522\t  before I eject the volcano!\"\n1523\t- *Win:* IGGY: \"You've got fire, Delgado. Here. Magma Cleats. They're only a little bit on fire.\" (Jet Cleats +1.)\n1524\t\n1525\t**Stop 3: Tranquility Dome vs the Meteors.**\n1526\t- *Pregame:* COSMO: \"Welcome to the Moon, Comets. Up here every pop fly is a field trip.\" HANK: \"Is there a snack bar\n1527\t  on the Moon?\" LOU: \"Gravity took the day off, folks. Somebody tell the baseball.\"\n1528\t- *First meteor shower:* HAP: \"Meteor shower in left field! The grounds crew is going to need a bigger rake!\"\n1529\t- *Win:* COSMO: \"Mission accomplished, for you. Zero-G Gloves. They catch whatever gravity drops.\" (Glue Gloves +1.)\n1530\t\n1531\t**Stop 4: Boneyard Ballpark vs the Haunts.**\n1532\t- *Pregame:* RATTLEBONES: \"We've been dying to play you. Literally. Since 1887.\" PIP: \"I'm not scared.\" PEP: \"You're\n1533\t  holding my hand.\" PIP: \"You're holding MINE.\"\n1534\t- *First Phantom Fog:* HAP: \"Where'd it go?! The ball just turned into a rumor!\"\n1535\t- *Win:* RATTLEBONES: \"A fine game, mortals. Phantom Pine Tar. It makes the crowd scream louder.\" (Hype Machine +1.)\n1536\t\n1537\t**Stop 5 (the final): the MegaMax MegaDome vs the Mechanicals, for the Kaboom Cup.**\n1538\t- *Pregame:* MORTIMER (on the MEGA-TRON): \"Meet my ace. Ninety thousand horsepower. Zero feelings. ENFORCER-9000!\"\n1539\t  ENFORCER: \"PREPARE. TO. BE. STRUCK. OUT.\" DOT: \"Then let's give him some feelings.\" IKE: \"Swing when they roar,\n1540\t  kid.\"\n1541\t- *First short circuit:* LOU: \"He's smoking! I mean really smoking! Somebody unplug that fella!\"\n1542\t- *Rally Cap* (if trailing in the last inning): HAP: \"Listen to this! The Krakens, the Eruptors, the Meteors, even\n1543\t  the Haunts! They're ALL chanting for the Comets!\" (meter → 100)\n1544\t- *Win, the ending:*\n1545\t  1. The Batzooka's last moonshot hits the MEGA-TRON, which rains sparks.\n1546\t  2. MORTIMER: \"My jumbotron! My deed! My... reputation!\"\n1547\t  3. The deed flutters into the Batzooka's backblast and burns to confetti.\n1548\t  4. DOT: \"Kernel Field stays. Same time next season?\"\n1549\t  5. ENFORCER: \"...I. LIKE. BASEBALL.\"\n1550\t  6. **Credits** roll over a blooper reel: rigs doing pratfalls, Hank eating, the mascot race tumble. Then \"THE END?\n1551\t     Exhibition: everything unlocked.\"\n1552\t- *Loss:* MORTIMER: \"Pave it! Pave it all!\" → RAIN CHECK.\n1553\t\n1554\t### 7.6 Spring Training lessons (`53-lessons.js`)\n1555\t\n1556\tEach lesson: Ike's intro (two lines), a drill with an on-screen goal (\"3 / 3 FAIR BALLS\"), prompts, and \"LESSON\n1557\tPASSED!\". Lessons 1–2 have slow motion ×0.6 on the first pitches.\n1558\t\n1559\t| # | Lesson | Drill | Passed when |\n1560\t|---|---|---|---|\n1561\t| 1 | **Batting Practice** | slow heaters from Ike; aim and time the contact swing | 3 fair balls |\n1562\t| 2 | **Power and Bunts** | power swings at meatballs, then bunt | 1 home run with a power swing and 1 fair bunt |\n1563\t| 3 | **Reading the Zone** | a mix of strikes and balls, curves included | take 2 balls and hit 2 strikes |\n1564\t| 4 | **On the Mound** | you pitch to a CPU batter | 3 strikes with 3 different pitches, one PERFECT release, one aftertouch |\n1565\t| 5 | **Leather and Lasers** | fielding: Ike hits flies and grounders | 2 fly catches, a grounder thrown to first in time, a double play |\n1566\t| 6 | **Wheels** | baserunning | advance on a hit, tag up on a fly, steal second, use turbo, slide in safe |\n1567\t| 7 | **BATZOOKA!** | the meter is pre-filled | hit a Batzooka home run, throw a super pitch, make a Laser Arm throw |\n1568\t| 8 | **Rhubarb 101** | a practice brawl with the grounds crew | land 5 punches, 1 shove and 1 toss |\n1569\t| – | **House Rules** card | what you can't do (§6.1) | – |\n1570\t\n1571\t### 7.7 Derby\n1572\t\n1573\tRules are in §6.18. Targets by park: the blimp (every park but the moon dome, which has a satellite instead), the\n1574\tjumbotron or scoreboard, the bullseye on the batter's eye, and drones at the MegaDome. The hub round uses the\n1575\tMegaDome.\n1576\t\n1577\t### 7.8 Clubhouse upgrades (`55-upgrades.js`)\n1578\t\n1579\t| Upgrade | Per tier | Costs (FB) for tiers 1 / 2 / 3 |\n1580\t|---|---|---|\n1581\t| Lumber | exit speed +5% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n1582\t| Glue Gloves | catch radius +1 U, catch chance +2% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n1583\t| Jet Cleats | run and field speed +4% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n1584\t| Cannon Arms | throws +5%, pitch speed +3% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n1585\t| Hype Machine | meter gain +10% | 500 / 1000 / 1600 |\n1586\t\n1587\tThe clubhouse screen is five big cards with a picture, the tier pips, the cost and \"✕ BUY\". Grandpa Ike comments on\n1588\teach purchase.\n1589\t\n1590\t### 7.9 Commentary line pools (`54-lines.js`)\n1591\t\n1592\tAt least 6 lines per tag (and 10 for the most common: strike, ball, foul, single, out). Samples in the voice to\n1593\tmatch:\n1594\t\n1595\t| Tag | Samples |\n1596\t|---|---|\n1597\t| `batter_up` (PA) | \"Now batting... number seven... DOT... DYNAMITE... DELGADO!\" |\n1598\t| `strike_called` | \"Strike one, right on the black. You could hang a picture on that one.\" |\n1599\t| `strike_swinging` | \"Swing and a miss! He swung so hard he unscrewed himself from the box!\" |\n1600\t| `ball` | \"Ball, low. That one was dragging its feet.\" |\n1601\t| `foul_back` | \"Fouled straight back! Duck, Lou!\" / LOU: \"I've been ducking since '79.\" |\n1602\t| `strikeout` | \"Strike three! Back to the dugout to think about what he's done.\" |\n1603\t| `walk` | \"Ball four. Take your base, and take a sandwich while you're at it.\" |\n1604\t| `single` | \"Seeing-eye single through the right side! That ball had a map and a flashlight.\" |\n1605\t| `double` | \"Into the gap! {batter} is digging for second like there's buried treasure!\" |\n1606\t| `triple` | \"Off the wall, he's rounding second, he's going for three! He's SAFE!\" |\n1607\t| `homer` | \"Swung on and BELTED! Deep! Way back! That ball has left the zip code!\" / \"{dist} feet! They'll need a passport to bring that one back!\" |\n1608\t| `batzooka_ready` | \"The crowd is ROARING! You know what that means... it's BATZOOKA TIME!\" |\n1609\t| `batzooka_hit` | \"KA-BLAMMO! That's not a home run, that's a space program!\" |\n1610\t| `batzooka_fizzle` | \"Fizzle! That's the loudest nothing I've ever heard.\" |\n1611\t| `super_pitch` | \"{pitcher} just threw a pitch that's probably illegal in three states!\" |\n1612\t| `catch_dive` | \"Laid out like a welcome mat! What a grab!\" |\n1613\t| `robbery` | \"He climbed the wall and STOLE it! Call the sheriff!\" |\n1614\t| `error` | \"Clank! You could hear that one in the next county.\" |\n1615\t| `double_play` | \"Two for the price of one! Around the horn and back for a nap!\" |\n1616\t| `steal_safe` | \"He's stealing! ...SAFE! Lock up your valuables, folks.\" |\n1617\t| `bowl_over` | \"COLLISION AT THE PLATE! Somebody check the catcher's warranty!\" |\n1618\t| `rhubarb_start` | \"Here come the benches! It's a rhubarb, folks, a genuine dust-up!\" |\n1619\t| `rhubarb_end` | \"Barb's breaking it up. Everybody's dusting off. Nobody's going home, though everybody's going home dirty.\" |\n1620\t| `walkoff` | \"WALK-OFF! The Comets win it! Pile on, pile on!\" |\n1621\t| `lead_change` | \"And just like that, we've got ourselves a brand-new ballgame!\" |\n1622\t| `hazard_*` | one pool per park (§7.5's first-time lines plus 5 more each) |\n1623\t| `between` | \"Time for the Mascot Race! My money's on the popcorn.\" |\n1624\t| `umpire` (stamps + voice) | \"STEE-RIIIKE!\" \"BALL!\" \"YER OUT!\" \"SAFE!\" \"FAIR BALL!\" \"FOUL!\" \"PLAY BALL!\" \"TIME!\" |\n1625\t| `vendor` | \"PEANUTS!\" \"GET YER DOGS!\" \"COLD LEMONADE!\" |\n1626\t\n1627\t### 7.10 Music\n1628\t\n1629\tThe list is in §6.16. Every song is written in the engine's notation in `56-songs.js` (a melody, bass and drums at\n1630\tleast; organ voicing for the ballpark tunes; named layers for in-game loops).\n1631\t\n1632\t### 7.11 Attract reel segments (`35-attract.js`)\n1633\t\n1634\t| # | Segment (caption) | Park | What's forced | ≈ s |\n1635\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1636\t| 1 | \"PLAY BALL!\" | Kernel Field | the title flyover, then a pitch duel in the Plate Cam: a called strike, a foul back, then a line-drive single and the throw in | 18 |\n1637\t| 2 | \"SUPER PITCHES\" | Caldera | Iggy's Meteor Heater for a swinging strike three; then a fly ball launched by a lava vent | 15 |\n1638\t| 3 | \"LEATHER AND LASERS\" | Barnacle Bay | a diving catch in right; a gull snatches a fly; a Laser Arm throw home, a slide and a bowl-over | 20 |\n1639\t| 4 | \"WHEELS\" | Kernel Field | a steal of second with a headfirst dive; turbo | 12 |\n1640\t| 5 | \"BATZOOKA!\" | MegaDome | Dot arms the Batzooka: the moonshot, the Moonshot Cam, the MEGA-TRON explodes, fireworks, the trot | 20 |\n1641\t| 6 | \"RHUBARB!\" | Caldera | HBP into the brawl: fight clouds; Barb breaks it up | 14 |\n1642\t| 7 | \"SIX WILD PARKS\" | Tranquility | a low-gravity fly; the CF climbs the wall 3× high for a robbery | 14 |\n1643\t| 8 | (continued) | Boneyard | the Banshee Ball (an invisible pitch) for a whiff; a ghost wall catch | 14 |\n1644\t| 9 | \"1–4 PLAYERS · PLAY ONLINE IN AI HUB\" | MegaDome | Derby swings with three ghost comets (local fakes) | 15 |\n1645\t| 10 | \"MOONSHOT LEADERS\" | – | the high-score table, then the title logo and \"PRESS START\" | 10 |\n1646\t\n1647\t### 7.12 Art assets to make (`04-shapes.js`, code-drawn sprites)\n1648\t\n1649\tUse the engine's core library where it fits (`barrel`, `crate`, `bench`, `fence`, `tree`, `pine`, `rock`, `bush`,\n1650\t`lamppost`, `sign`, `cart`, `table`) and props (`lamp`, `streetlamp`, `banner`, `flag`, `torch`, `candle`, `lantern`,\n1651\t`pot`, `skull`, `cobweb`). Write new `E.SHAPES` entries (check each with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`) for:\n1652\t- **Every park:** the base (a white pillow), home plate, the rubber, the mound, the foul pole, the dugout bench, the\n1653\t  bat rack, the helmet rack, the water cooler, the rosin bag, a light tower (with `lights:`), a scoreboard frame, the\n1654\t  jumbotron frame, the batting-practice L-screen, the batting cage net, the Pitch-O-Matic 3000.\n1655\t- **Kernel Field:** cornstalk, silo, hay bale, red-barn scoreboard, windmill, windsock.\n1656\t- **Barnacle Bay:** lighthouse, boat, buoy, pier piling, lobster trap.\n1657\t- **Caldera:** basalt column, lava vent (cone, with glow), warning sign.\n1658\t- **Tranquility:** habitat module, antenna, satellite dish, rover, airlock.\n1659\t- **Boneyard:** tombstone (3 shapes by seed), crypt, iron fence section, jack-o'-lantern.\n1660\t- **MegaDome:** holo-billboard, drone, luxury box, MEGA-TRON.\n1661\t\n1662\t**Code-drawn sprites:** the ball (5×5, with stitches, 2 rotating frames), the blimp, gulls (a Blob with wings), the\n1663\tlanding marker, the reticles (contact: a thin ring; power: a thick red ring; Batzooka: a ring of fire), the pitch\n1664\ttarget and release ring, the zone grid, base rings, the glyph icons (§6.13), the meter gauges, the scorebug, the\n1665\tBatzooka overdraw (nozzle, fins and a glowing barrel over the bat in the hands), the fight cloud, popcorn, confetti\n1666\tand fireworks.\n1667\t\n1668\t---\n1669\t\n1670\t## 8. Art and animation\n1671\t\n1672\t### 8.1 Look (the engine's own look target, applied)\n1673\t\n1674\t1. **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`. The HUD anchors to `r.W` and `r.H`. Rigs are `size: 1.15–1.35`\n1675\t   (bosses 2.2); props use `propSize: 1.3`.\n1676\t2. **Dressed characters:** every player gets the team uniform, plus hair, skin, build and size of their own, and the\n1677\t   gear for their job (below). Nobody keeps the defaults."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"8fcb93a5-e0bf-42c3-bc3c-c9061ef2abdd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:38:28.013Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work/PLAN.md","content":"- → Offer Spring Training (\"Learn the ropes with Grandpa Ike?\" PLAY · SKIP), then the Tour Map.\n\n**Stop 1: Barnacle Bay Park vs the Krakens.**\n- *Pregame:* BRINE: \"Ahoy, corn-pickers! The tide's coming in, and it's bringing a whole ocean of hurt!\" DOT: \"We\n  brought sunscreen.\" LOU: \"Watch the gulls, folks. They've got better hands than my old infield.\"\n- *First gull snatch:* HAP: \"A seagull just stole a fly ball! Is that legal? Barb says it's... in play!\"\n- *Win:* BRINE: \"Blast it all. Take this. Barnacle Grip Tape. Sticks to anything, except a lead.\" (Lumber +1.)\n- *Loss:* BRINE: \"Back to the shallow end, landlubbers!\"\n\n**Stop 2: Caldera Field vs the Eruptors.**\n- *Pregame:* IGGY: \"Hope you packed sunscreen. SPF one million.\" IKE: \"Don't stand on anything that's glowing.\"\n- *First vent:* HAP: \"The ground just sneezed lava, and the baseball went with it!\"\n- *Scripted Rhubarb* (the first time Iggy hits a batter, or in the 2nd inning by script): LOU: \"Uh-oh, the benches\n  are emptying! Somebody fetch a fire extinguisher and a referee!\" BARB (after): \"Everybody back in your dugouts\n  before I eject the volcano!\"\n- *Win:* IGGY: \"You've got fire, Delgado. Here. Magma Cleats. They're only a little bit on fire.\" (Jet Cleats +1.)\n\n**Stop 3: Tranquility Dome vs the Meteors.**\n- *Pregame:* COSMO: \"Welcome to the Moon, Comets. Up here every pop fly is a field trip.\" HANK: \"Is there a snack bar\n  on the Moon?\" LOU: \"Gravity took the day off, folks. Somebody tell the baseball.\"\n- *First meteor shower:* HAP: \"Meteor shower in left field! The grounds crew is going to need a bigger rake!\"\n- *Win:* COSMO: \"Mission accomplished, for you. Zero-G Gloves. They catch whatever gravity drops.\" (Glue Gloves +1.)\n\n**Stop 4: Boneyard Ballpark vs the Haunts.**\n- *Pregame:* RATTLEBONES: \"We've been dying to play you. Literally. Since 1887.\" PIP: \"I'm not scared.\" PEP: \"You're\n  holding my hand.\" PIP: \"You're holding MINE.\"\n- *First Phantom Fog:* HAP: \"Where'd it go?! The ball just turned into a rumor!\"\n- *Win:* RATTLEBONES: \"A fine game, mortals. Phantom Pine Tar. It makes the crowd scream louder.\" (Hype Machine +1.)\n\n**Stop 5 (the final): the MegaMax MegaDome vs the Mechanicals, for the Kaboom Cup.**\n- *Pregame:* MORTIMER (on the MEGA-TRON): \"Meet my ace. Ninety thousand horsepower. Zero feelings. ENFORCER-9000!\"\n  ENFORCER: \"PREPARE. TO. BE. STRUCK. OUT.\" DOT: \"Then let's give him some feelings.\" IKE: \"Swing when they roar,\n  kid.\"\n- *First short circuit:* LOU: \"He's smoking! I mean really smoking! Somebody unplug that fella!\"\n- *Rally Cap* (if trailing in the last inning): HAP: \"Listen to this! The Krakens, the Eruptors, the Meteors, even\n  the Haunts! They're ALL chanting for the Comets!\" (meter → 100)\n- *Win, the ending:*\n  1. The Batzooka's last moonshot hits the MEGA-TRON, which rains sparks.\n  2. MORTIMER: \"My jumbotron! My deed! My... reputation!\"\n  3. The deed flutters into the Batzooka's backblast and burns to confetti.\n  4. DOT: \"Kernel Field stays. Same time next season?\"\n  5. ENFORCER: \"...I. LIKE. BASEBALL.\"\n  6. **Credits** roll over a blooper reel: rigs doing pratfalls, Hank eating, the mascot race tumble. Then \"THE END?\n     Exhibition: everything unlocked.\"\n- *Loss:* MORTIMER: \"Pave it! Pave it all!\" → RAIN CHECK.\n\n### 7.6 Spring Training lessons (`53-lessons.js`)\n\nEach lesson: Ike's intro (two lines), a drill with an on-screen goal (\"3 / 3 FAIR BALLS\"), prompts, and \"LESSON\nPASSED!\". Lessons 1–2 have slow motion ×0.6 on the first pitches.\n\n| # | Lesson | Drill | Passed when |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Batting Practice** | slow heaters from Ike; aim and time the contact swing | 3 fair balls |\n| 2 | **Power and Bunts** | power swings at meatballs, then bunt | 1 home run with a power swing and 1 fair bunt |\n| 3 | **Reading the Zone** | a mix of strikes and balls, curves included | take 2 balls and hit 2 strikes |\n| 4 | **On the Mound** | you pitch to a CPU batter | 3 strikes with 3 different pitches, one PERFECT release, one aftertouch |\n| 5 | **Leather and Lasers** | fielding: Ike hits flies and grounders | 2 fly catches, a grounder thrown to first in time, a double play |\n| 6 | **Wheels** | baserunning | advance on a hit, tag up on a fly, steal second, use turbo, slide in safe |\n| 7 | **BATZOOKA!** | the meter is pre-filled | hit a Batzooka home run, throw a super pitch, make a Laser Arm throw |\n| 8 | **Rhubarb 101** | a practice brawl with the grounds crew | land 5 punches, 1 shove and 1 toss |\n| – | **House Rules** card | what you can't do (§6.1) | – |\n\n### 7.7 Derby\n\nRules are in §6.18. Targets by park: the blimp (every park but the moon dome, which has a satellite instead), the\njumbotron or scoreboard, the bullseye on the batter's eye, and drones at the MegaDome. The hub round uses the\nMegaDome.\n\n### 7.8 Clubhouse upgrades (`55-upgrades.js`)\n\n| Upgrade | Per tier | Costs (FB) for tiers 1 / 2 / 3 |\n|---|---|---|\n| Lumber | exit speed +5% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n| Glue Gloves | catch radius +1 U, catch chance +2% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n| Jet Cleats | run and field speed +4% | 300 / 700 / 1200 |\n| Cannon Arms | throws +5%, pitch speed +3% | 400 / 800 / 1400 |\n| Hype Machine | meter gain +10% | 500 / 1000 / 1600 |\n\nThe clubhouse screen is five big cards with a picture, the tier pips, the cost and \"✕ BUY\". Grandpa Ike comments on\neach purchase.\n\n### 7.9 Commentary line pools (`54-lines.js`)\n\nAt least 6 lines per tag (and 10 for the most common: strike, ball, foul, single, out). Samples in the voice to\nmatch:\n\n| Tag | Samples |\n|---|---|\n| `batter_up` (PA) | \"Now batting... number seven... DOT... DYNAMITE... DELGADO!\" |\n| `strike_called` | \"Strike one, right on the black. You could hang a picture on that one.\" |\n| `strike_swinging` | \"Swing and a miss! He swung so hard he unscrewed himself from the box!\" |\n| `ball` | \"Ball, low. That one was dragging its feet.\" |\n| `foul_back` | \"Fouled straight back! Duck, Lou!\" / LOU: \"I've been ducking since '79.\" |\n| `strikeout` | \"Strike three! Back to the dugout to think about what he's done.\" |\n| `walk` | \"Ball four. Take your base, and take a sandwich while you're at it.\" |\n| `single` | \"Seeing-eye single through the right side! That ball had a map and a flashlight.\" |\n| `double` | \"Into the gap! {batter} is digging for second like there's buried treasure!\" |\n| `triple` | \"Off the wall, he's rounding second, he's going for three! He's SAFE!\" |\n| `homer` | \"Swung on and BELTED! Deep! Way back! That ball has left the zip code!\" / \"{dist} feet! They'll need a passport to bring that one back!\" |\n| `batzooka_ready` | \"The crowd is ROARING! You know what that means... it's BATZOOKA TIME!\" |\n| `batzooka_hit` | \"KA-BLAMMO! That's not a home run, that's a space program!\" |\n| `batzooka_fizzle` | \"Fizzle! That's the loudest nothing I've ever heard.\" |\n| `super_pitch` | \"{pitcher} just threw a pitch that's probably illegal in three states!\" |\n| `catch_dive` | \"Laid out like a welcome mat! What a grab!\" |\n| `robbery` | \"He climbed the wall and STOLE it! Call the sheriff!\" |\n| `error` | \"Clank! You could hear that one in the next county.\" |\n| `double_play` | \"Two for the price of one! Around the horn and back for a nap!\" |\n| `steal_safe` | \"He's stealing! ...SAFE! Lock up your valuables, folks.\" |\n| `bowl_over` | \"COLLISION AT THE PLATE! Somebody check the catcher's warranty!\" |\n| `rhubarb_start` | \"Here come the benches! It's a rhubarb, folks, a genuine dust-up!\" |\n| `rhubarb_end` | \"Barb's breaking it up. Everybody's dusting off. Nobody's going home, though everybody's going home dirty.\" |\n| `walkoff` | \"WALK-OFF! The Comets win it! Pile on, pile on!\" |\n| `lead_change` | \"And just like that, we've got ourselves a brand-new ballgame!\" |\n| `hazard_*` | one pool per park (§7.5's first-time lines plus 5 more each) |\n| `between` | \"Time for the Mascot Race! My money's on the popcorn.\" |\n| `umpire` (stamps + voice) | \"STEE-RIIIKE!\" \"BALL!\" \"YER OUT!\" \"SAFE!\" \"FAIR BALL!\" \"FOUL!\" \"PLAY BALL!\" \"TIME!\" |\n| `vendor` | \"PEANUTS!\" \"GET YER DOGS!\" \"COLD LEMONADE!\" |\n\n### 7.10 Music\n\nThe list is in §6.16. Every song is written in the engine's notation in `56-songs.js` (a melody, bass and drums at\nleast; organ voicing for the ballpark tunes; named layers for in-game loops).\n\n### 7.11 Attract reel segments (`35-attract.js`)\n\n| # | Segment (caption) | Park | What's forced | ≈ s |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"PLAY BALL!\" | Kernel Field | the title flyover, then a pitch duel in the Plate Cam: a called strike, a foul back, then a line-drive single and the throw in | 18 |\n| 2 | \"SUPER PITCHES\" | Caldera | Iggy's Meteor Heater for a swinging strike three; then a fly ball launched by a lava vent | 15 |\n| 3 | \"LEATHER AND LASERS\" | Barnacle Bay | a diving catch in right; a gull snatches a fly; a Laser Arm throw home, a slide and a bowl-over | 20 |\n| 4 | \"WHEELS\" | Kernel Field | a steal of second with a headfirst dive; turbo | 12 |\n| 5 | \"BATZOOKA!\" | MegaDome | Dot arms the Batzooka: the moonshot, the Moonshot Cam, the MEGA-TRON explodes, fireworks, the trot | 20 |\n| 6 | \"RHUBARB!\" | Caldera | HBP into the brawl: fight clouds; Barb breaks it up | 14 |\n| 7 | \"SIX WILD PARKS\" | Tranquility | a low-gravity fly; the CF climbs the wall 3× high for a robbery | 14 |\n| 8 | (continued) | Boneyard | the Banshee Ball (an invisible pitch) for a whiff; a ghost wall catch | 14 |\n| 9 | \"1–4 PLAYERS · PLAY ONLINE IN AI HUB\" | MegaDome | Derby swings with three ghost comets (local fakes) | 15 |\n| 10 | \"MOONSHOT LEADERS\" | – | the high-score table, then the title logo and \"PRESS START\" | 10 |\n\n### 7.12 Art assets to make (`04-shapes.js`, code-drawn sprites)\n\nUse the engine's core library where it fits (`barrel`, `crate`, `bench`, `fence`, `tree`, `pine`, `rock`, `bush`,\n`lamppost`, `sign`, `cart`, `table`) and props (`lamp`, `streetlamp`, `banner`, `flag`, `torch`, `candle`, `lantern`,\n`pot`, `skull`, `cobweb`). Write new `E.SHAPES` entries (check each with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`) for:\n- **Every park:** the base (a white pillow), home plate, the rubber, the mound, the foul pole, the dugout bench, the\n  bat rack, the helmet rack, the water cooler, the rosin bag, a light tower (with `lights:`), a scoreboard frame, the\n  jumbotron frame, the batting-practice L-screen, the batting cage net, the Pitch-O-Matic 3000.\n- **Kernel Field:** cornstalk, silo, hay bale, red-barn scoreboard, windmill, windsock.\n- **Barnacle Bay:** lighthouse, boat, buoy, pier piling, lobster trap.\n- **Caldera:** basalt column, lava vent (cone, with glow), warning sign.\n- **Tranquility:** habitat module, antenna, satellite dish, rover, airlock.\n- **Boneyard:** tombstone (3 shapes by seed), crypt, iron fence section, jack-o'-lantern.\n- **MegaDome:** holo-billboard, drone, luxury box, MEGA-TRON.\n\n**Code-drawn sprites:** the ball (5×5, with stitches, 2 rotating frames), the blimp, gulls (a Blob with wings), the\nlanding marker, the reticles (contact: a thin ring; power: a thick red ring; Batzooka: a ring of fire), the pitch\ntarget and release ring, the zone grid, base rings, the glyph icons (§6.13), the meter gauges, the scorebug, the\nBatzooka overdraw (nozzle, fins and a glowing barrel over the bat in the hands), the fight cloud, popcorn, confetti\nand fireworks.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Art and animation\n\n### 8.1 Look (the engine's own look target, applied)\n\n1. **Resolution:** `res: 'ps1'`, `expand: true`. The HUD anchors to `r.W` and `r.H`. Rigs are `size: 1.15–1.35`\n   (bosses 2.2); props use `propSize: 1.3`.\n2. **Dressed characters:** every player gets the team uniform, plus hair, skin, build and size of their own, and the\n   gear for their job (below). Nobody keeps the defaults.","numLines":170,"startLine":1508,"totalLines":2123}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F3ed9Y6rpVLVc5cUutLRFd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
