{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XNkmZeRNpdJqNUJRERW5v9","type":"tool_result","content":"1677\t   gear for their job (below). Nobody keeps the defaults.\n1678\t3. **Backdrops:** every park's sky is an `E.Backdrop` (§7.2), seen in the Plate Cam and the Moonshot Cam. The Broadcast\n1679\t   Cam shows ground to the screen's edges (the park continues past the stands; `map.outside` is the park's ground\n1680\t   color).\n1681\t4. **Textures:** grass with grain and a mow pattern, dirt with speckle, chalk lines slightly worn, the warning track,\n1682\t   padded fence faces, stone or plank stands.\n1683\t5. **Props on every screen:** dugouts, bat racks, coolers, light towers, poles, the park's own pieces (§7.12), 3–8 in\n1684\t   any Broadcast Cam view.\n1685\t6. **Effects on every hit** (§8.4).\n1686\t7. **Color:** everything drawn by hand is shaded with `E.tones` and `E.ramp`.\n1687\t8. **Type:** the `E.font.title` logo and stamps; HUD text with shadows; `E.ui.box` gradient panels.\n1688\t9. **Light:** night parks run `game.lights` with tower floods and local glows; day parks a warm high ambient.\n1689\t   Emissive for fire, neon, lasers and the Batzooka.\n1690\t10. **Faces in dialog:** every speaker has a live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), the announcers included.\n1691\t\n1692\t### 8.2 Rigs and uniforms (`03-rigs.js`)\n1693\t\n1694\t`BZ.makeRig(player, team, job)` builds an `E.Humanoid` from the team's colors and the player's looks:\n1695\t\n1696\t| Job | Kit |\n1697\t|---|---|\n1698\t| batter | `hat: 'batting'` in the team color, `weapon: 'bat'`, `grip: 'both'`, batting gloves (`colors.glove`) |\n1699\t| fielder | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` (`'first'` for 1B) |\n1700\t| catcher | `hat: 'mask'`, `armor: true` (the chest protector, `plate` = the team's dark color), `mitt: 'catcher'` |\n1701\t| pitcher | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` |\n1702\t| runner | `hat: 'batting'`, no bat |\n1703\t| umpire | `outfit: 'coat'` (navy), `hat: 'mask'` |\n1704\t| robots | metal colors, `eyeGlow`, a stiffer gait (`stride` and `swing` lower), sparks when short-circuited |\n1705\t| skeletons | `build: 'skeleton'`, `colors.bone` |\n1706\t| mascots, gulls, ghosts, drones | `E.Blob` (`feet`, `wings`, `mouth`, `face: 'front'`) |\n1707\t\n1708\tRigs are cached per player and job and swapped as the job changes (batter → runner → fielder between halves).\n1709\t\n1710\t### 8.3 New animations\n1711\t\n1712\t**Motion clips.** One set file, `assets/mocap-batzooka.js`:\n1713\t```\n1714\tnode tools/anim-set.mjs <repo>/src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js <repo>/examples/cmu-lib/CMU_124.js <repo>/src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js \\\n1715\t  --clips 124_01,124_07,124_08,124_12,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Jab,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Cross,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands \\\n1716\t  --name BATZOOKA --out assets/mocap-batzooka.js\n1717\t```\n1718\tIf a clip name is reported as in two sets, prefix it with `SET:`, as the tool asks. Load `engine/mocap-readable.js`,\n1719\t`engine/mocap.js` and the set after the engine. Then:\n1720\t- `const lib = Mocap.load(MOCAP.BATZOOKA)`, and `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` once per rig that uses clips.\n1721\t- The CMU takes are long, with several repetitions. Write `tools/clip-windows.mjs` to find one clean window per motion\n1722\t  (the hands' speed peak marks contact or release; the window runs from the last still moment before it to the next\n1723\t  one after it) and store them as data: `{ swing: ['124_07', a, b, contactAt], pitch: ['124_01', a, b, releaseAt], ... }`.\n1724\t- Time-map each window so that its contact or release key lands exactly on the game's moment (the swing delay, the\n1725\t  release time).\n1726\t- `rig.mocapW` fades in and out over 0.08 s. Lefties use `MocapReadable.mirror(clip)`, made once at load.\n1727\t- The bat follows the hands (`rig.mocapBlade = true`, with the `bat` weapon drawn along the knuckle line).\n1728\t- Review every motion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` on the `#gallery` page. If a clip reads badly at game size, use the\n1729\t  procedural fallback in the table (both are written, and the better one is picked by looking at the strips).\n1730\t\n1731\t| Motion | Source | Notes |\n1732\t|---|---|---|\n1733\t| batting stance and waggle | procedural: the bat up and back, knees bent (`crouch` .3), the bat bobbing on a sine with a per-player tempo | |\n1734\t| contact swing | clip 124_07 window, time-mapped to 0.10 s to the plane | fallback spec `SWING`: `{ rel: true, hand: 'both', a0: 2.4, a1: −2.6, z0: −2, z1: −4, reach: 6, wind: .10, active: .08, recover: .30, lunge: 2.2, twist: 2.2, lean: .25, hold: .35 }` |\n1735\t| power swing | the same window, stretched to 0.14 s, with a bigger stride (root forward 3 U) | fallback: `SWING` with lunge 3, twist 2.8 |\n1736\t| Batzooka swing | the power swing plus a recoil hop (`rig.kick`), muzzle flash and smoke | |\n1737\t| bunt | clip 124_08 window | fallback: the bat held level at the chest with both hands (an IK override) |\n1738\t| windup and pitch | clip 124_01 window (set, leg lift, stride, release, follow-through); mirrored for lefties; the ball leaves `rig.hand()` at the release key | fallback: the `knee` kick spec (leg lift) chained into `throw` (lunge 2.4, lean .6) |\n1739\t| underhand toss (Ike's batting practice, Derby intro) | clip 124_12 | |\n1740\t| fielder's throw | `E.MOVES.throw` plus a crow-hop for outfielders (`hop: .8`) | |\n1741\t| catch high, low and backhand | procedural: after `solvePose`, IK the glove hand to the ball (`E.ik3`); the body turns to it | |\n1742\t| dive | procedural: lean forward and blend `down` 0→1 over 0.2 s while the body slides; the glove reaches out | |\n1743\t| jump catch | `Body.jump` plus `air: true` and the glove IK'd up | |\n1744\t| wall climb | `climb: true` with vz (hand-over-hand) facing the fence; a reach at the top | |\n1745\t| feet-first slide | clips Slide_Start → Slide_Loop → Slide_Exit | |\n1746\t| headfirst dive | procedural: `down` blend, forward lean, both arms out | |\n1747\t| run and turbo | the engine's gait from velocity; turbo uses `sprint: true` (lean) plus speed lines | |\n1748\t| tag | a low swipe with the glove hand (custom spec, `hand: 'L'`) | |\n1749\t| umpire calls | strike: a right-fist punch-out (`cross` with a long `hold`) and `expr: 'shout'`; out: a fist pump (`uppercut`); safe: both arms sweeping out wide (a two-hand spec: a0 1.4 → a1 −0.2) | |\n1750\t| celebrations | clips Victory and Cheering_Two_Hands; `pose: 'cheer'`; high-fives (two rigs meeting); the dugout bounce | |\n1751\t| dejection | `pose: 'kneel'`, `expr: 'wince'` | |\n1752\t| Rhubarb | `E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook'])` (or clips Punch_Jab and Punch_Cross), `bash`, `throw`, `down` with dizzy stars | |\n1753\t| catcher | the `crouch` pose; the mitt IK'd to the pitch; popping up to throw | |\n1754\t| walk-up | walking with the bat on the shoulder; two practice swings | |\n1755\t| the trot | a jog; high-fives with the base coaches; a cap tip | |\n1756\t\n1757\t### 8.4 Effects\n1758\t\n1759\t- **Contact:** sparks and a ring by Q, a white flash 0.06 s, hit-stop 0.06 s, rumble.\n1760\t- **Broken bat:** on jammed contact (Q < 0.15 against a heater at 1.0× or more, 8% chance from `rng.fx`; cosmetic\n1761\t  only), wood splinters (`particles.bits` in wood colors) and \"CRACK! Broken bat!\" on the radio.\n1762\t- **Pitch trails:** speed lines for heaters; fire for the Meteor Heater; a wave sprite for the Tidal Wave; a dark\n1763\t  swirl for the Black Hole; a shimmer while invisible; a laser line for the Overclock Laser (emissive); popcorn puffs\n1764\t  for the Corn Popper.\n1765\t- **Ball:** a trail above 500 U/s; dust on bounces; sparks off the fence; a splash in water; a lava sizzle; a meteor\n1766\t  crater decal.\n1767\t- **Players:** dust on slides and dives; speed lines on turbo; fire trails for Afterburners; stars and a ring on\n1768\t  collisions; dizzy stars.\n1769\t- **Spectacle:** fireworks (`particles.explosion` small, plus colored sparks), confetti, popcorn, the crowd wave,\n1770\t  scoreboard bulbs, the jumbotron, heat shimmer at Caldera.\n1771\t- **Comfort:** every `shake` and `flash` follows the comfort settings.\n1772\t\n1773\t---\n1774\t\n1775\t## 9. Build order and milestones\n1776\t\n1777\tBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`), the bundle building, and a\n1778\tplayable build. Temporary scaffolding inside a milestone is fine, but nothing temporary survives M8.\n1779\t\n1780\t**M0: Foundation.**\n1781\t- Make the dev folder (§4.1) and fetch the sources (§3.1).\n1782\t- `npm install`, then `npx playwright install chromium`. If `/tmp` is full on this shared machine (it was while\n1783\t  planning), run Playwright and Chromium with `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n1784\t- Write `tools/build.mjs` (concat `src/` into `build/game.js`; bundle `../BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html` per §12).\n1785\t- Write `tests/run.mjs` and the headless loader (§11.2); `index.html`; the `00-core` spine (registries, bus, RNG,\n1786\t  TUNE); the boot, title and match scene skeletons; the `game.debug` skeleton.\n1787\t- Make engine changes 1, 2, 4 and 5 (§3.3) and look at the bat and mitt in the gallery.\n1788\t- **Done when:** the bundle opens to a title in `tools/check.mjs` with no errors, the smoke test passes, and the\n1789\t  gallery shows a rig holding a bat and wearing a mitt.\n1790\t\n1791\t**M1: The at-bat** (the core, and the biggest risk; §10 R1 and R2).\n1792\t- Field geometry and the Kernel Field TileMap; the Plate Cam with the fence, stands and towers.\n1793\t- The pitcher, batter and catcher rigs with clips or fallbacks.\n1794\t- Pitch types, windup, release ring, aftertouch; the reticle, swings and contact model; the count rules and calls.\n1795\t- Batted-ball physics with home run, foul and fair detection; the Broadcast Cam showing the ball's flight.\n1796\t- Umpire stamps, basic sounds, the timing feedback and the dev timing bar.\n1797\t- For this milestone only, a ball in play resolves at its landing as a \"HIT!\" or \"OUT!\" stamp by a simple rule. M3\n1798\t  replaces this with real fielding.\n1799\t- **Done when:** T-PITCH, T-BAT, T-BALL and T-RULES (the count part) pass; at-bats against the CPU are fun in a quick\n1800\t  self-play check; Plate Cam screenshots at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 show a readable zone, batter, pitcher and ball.\n1801\t\n1802\t**M2: The Derby and the AI Hub** (early, to settle the protocol and the bundle; §10 R7 and R8).\n1803\t- The Derby: local play with 1–4 players hot seat, targets, scoring, the initials table.\n1804\t- `40-hub.js`: connect, our card, ready, start, progress, result, time-up, end, ghosts.\n1805\t- The session rules, the meta tags, and the session client placement in the bundle.\n1806\t- **Done when:** T-DERBY and T-HUB pass headless and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true in the real harness for `players=2&auto=1`,\n1807\t  `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1` and `&scenario=host-leave`; the bundle still opens normally outside\n1808\t  a hub.\n1809\t\n1810\t**M3: Fielding, running and the full game.**\n1811\t- Fielders (assignment, chase, catch, throw, cutoffs, tags, forces, rundowns); baserunners (forces, tag-ups, orders,"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"4082dac9-c27a-4462-92e6-f684200b492d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:38:48.247Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work/PLAN.md","content":"   gear for their job (below). Nobody keeps the defaults.\n3. **Backdrops:** every park's sky is an `E.Backdrop` (§7.2), seen in the Plate Cam and the Moonshot Cam. The Broadcast\n   Cam shows ground to the screen's edges (the park continues past the stands; `map.outside` is the park's ground\n   color).\n4. **Textures:** grass with grain and a mow pattern, dirt with speckle, chalk lines slightly worn, the warning track,\n   padded fence faces, stone or plank stands.\n5. **Props on every screen:** dugouts, bat racks, coolers, light towers, poles, the park's own pieces (§7.12), 3–8 in\n   any Broadcast Cam view.\n6. **Effects on every hit** (§8.4).\n7. **Color:** everything drawn by hand is shaded with `E.tones` and `E.ramp`.\n8. **Type:** the `E.font.title` logo and stamps; HUD text with shadows; `E.ui.box` gradient panels.\n9. **Light:** night parks run `game.lights` with tower floods and local glows; day parks a warm high ambient.\n   Emissive for fire, neon, lasers and the Batzooka.\n10. **Faces in dialog:** every speaker has a live portrait (`rig.drawPortrait`), the announcers included.\n\n### 8.2 Rigs and uniforms (`03-rigs.js`)\n\n`BZ.makeRig(player, team, job)` builds an `E.Humanoid` from the team's colors and the player's looks:\n\n| Job | Kit |\n|---|---|\n| batter | `hat: 'batting'` in the team color, `weapon: 'bat'`, `grip: 'both'`, batting gloves (`colors.glove`) |\n| fielder | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` (`'first'` for 1B) |\n| catcher | `hat: 'mask'`, `armor: true` (the chest protector, `plate` = the team's dark color), `mitt: 'catcher'` |\n| pitcher | `hat: 'cap'`, `mitt: 'fielder'` |\n| runner | `hat: 'batting'`, no bat |\n| umpire | `outfit: 'coat'` (navy), `hat: 'mask'` |\n| robots | metal colors, `eyeGlow`, a stiffer gait (`stride` and `swing` lower), sparks when short-circuited |\n| skeletons | `build: 'skeleton'`, `colors.bone` |\n| mascots, gulls, ghosts, drones | `E.Blob` (`feet`, `wings`, `mouth`, `face: 'front'`) |\n\nRigs are cached per player and job and swapped as the job changes (batter → runner → fielder between halves).\n\n### 8.3 New animations\n\n**Motion clips.** One set file, `assets/mocap-batzooka.js`:\n```\nnode tools/anim-set.mjs <repo>/src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js <repo>/examples/cmu-lib/CMU_124.js <repo>/src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js \\\n  --clips 124_01,124_07,124_08,124_12,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Jab,QUATERNIUS:Punch_Cross,Victory,Cheering_Two_Hands \\\n  --name BATZOOKA --out assets/mocap-batzooka.js\n```\nIf a clip name is reported as in two sets, prefix it with `SET:`, as the tool asks. Load `engine/mocap-readable.js`,\n`engine/mocap.js` and the set after the engine. Then:\n- `const lib = Mocap.load(MOCAP.BATZOOKA)`, and `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` once per rig that uses clips.\n- The CMU takes are long, with several repetitions. Write `tools/clip-windows.mjs` to find one clean window per motion\n  (the hands' speed peak marks contact or release; the window runs from the last still moment before it to the next\n  one after it) and store them as data: `{ swing: ['124_07', a, b, contactAt], pitch: ['124_01', a, b, releaseAt], ... }`.\n- Time-map each window so that its contact or release key lands exactly on the game's moment (the swing delay, the\n  release time).\n- `rig.mocapW` fades in and out over 0.08 s. Lefties use `MocapReadable.mirror(clip)`, made once at load.\n- The bat follows the hands (`rig.mocapBlade = true`, with the `bat` weapon drawn along the knuckle line).\n- Review every motion with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` on the `#gallery` page. If a clip reads badly at game size, use the\n  procedural fallback in the table (both are written, and the better one is picked by looking at the strips).\n\n| Motion | Source | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| batting stance and waggle | procedural: the bat up and back, knees bent (`crouch` .3), the bat bobbing on a sine with a per-player tempo | |\n| contact swing | clip 124_07 window, time-mapped to 0.10 s to the plane | fallback spec `SWING`: `{ rel: true, hand: 'both', a0: 2.4, a1: −2.6, z0: −2, z1: −4, reach: 6, wind: .10, active: .08, recover: .30, lunge: 2.2, twist: 2.2, lean: .25, hold: .35 }` |\n| power swing | the same window, stretched to 0.14 s, with a bigger stride (root forward 3 U) | fallback: `SWING` with lunge 3, twist 2.8 |\n| Batzooka swing | the power swing plus a recoil hop (`rig.kick`), muzzle flash and smoke | |\n| bunt | clip 124_08 window | fallback: the bat held level at the chest with both hands (an IK override) |\n| windup and pitch | clip 124_01 window (set, leg lift, stride, release, follow-through); mirrored for lefties; the ball leaves `rig.hand()` at the release key | fallback: the `knee` kick spec (leg lift) chained into `throw` (lunge 2.4, lean .6) |\n| underhand toss (Ike's batting practice, Derby intro) | clip 124_12 | |\n| fielder's throw | `E.MOVES.throw` plus a crow-hop for outfielders (`hop: .8`) | |\n| catch high, low and backhand | procedural: after `solvePose`, IK the glove hand to the ball (`E.ik3`); the body turns to it | |\n| dive | procedural: lean forward and blend `down` 0→1 over 0.2 s while the body slides; the glove reaches out | |\n| jump catch | `Body.jump` plus `air: true` and the glove IK'd up | |\n| wall climb | `climb: true` with vz (hand-over-hand) facing the fence; a reach at the top | |\n| feet-first slide | clips Slide_Start → Slide_Loop → Slide_Exit | |\n| headfirst dive | procedural: `down` blend, forward lean, both arms out | |\n| run and turbo | the engine's gait from velocity; turbo uses `sprint: true` (lean) plus speed lines | |\n| tag | a low swipe with the glove hand (custom spec, `hand: 'L'`) | |\n| umpire calls | strike: a right-fist punch-out (`cross` with a long `hold`) and `expr: 'shout'`; out: a fist pump (`uppercut`); safe: both arms sweeping out wide (a two-hand spec: a0 1.4 → a1 −0.2) | |\n| celebrations | clips Victory and Cheering_Two_Hands; `pose: 'cheer'`; high-fives (two rigs meeting); the dugout bounce | |\n| dejection | `pose: 'kneel'`, `expr: 'wince'` | |\n| Rhubarb | `E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook'])` (or clips Punch_Jab and Punch_Cross), `bash`, `throw`, `down` with dizzy stars | |\n| catcher | the `crouch` pose; the mitt IK'd to the pitch; popping up to throw | |\n| walk-up | walking with the bat on the shoulder; two practice swings | |\n| the trot | a jog; high-fives with the base coaches; a cap tip | |\n\n### 8.4 Effects\n\n- **Contact:** sparks and a ring by Q, a white flash 0.06 s, hit-stop 0.06 s, rumble.\n- **Broken bat:** on jammed contact (Q < 0.15 against a heater at 1.0× or more, 8% chance from `rng.fx`; cosmetic\n  only), wood splinters (`particles.bits` in wood colors) and \"CRACK! Broken bat!\" on the radio.\n- **Pitch trails:** speed lines for heaters; fire for the Meteor Heater; a wave sprite for the Tidal Wave; a dark\n  swirl for the Black Hole; a shimmer while invisible; a laser line for the Overclock Laser (emissive); popcorn puffs\n  for the Corn Popper.\n- **Ball:** a trail above 500 U/s; dust on bounces; sparks off the fence; a splash in water; a lava sizzle; a meteor\n  crater decal.\n- **Players:** dust on slides and dives; speed lines on turbo; fire trails for Afterburners; stars and a ring on\n  collisions; dizzy stars.\n- **Spectacle:** fireworks (`particles.explosion` small, plus colored sparks), confetti, popcorn, the crowd wave,\n  scoreboard bulbs, the jumbotron, heat shimmer at Caldera.\n- **Comfort:** every `shake` and `flash` follows the comfort settings.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Build order and milestones\n\nBuild in this order. Each milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tests/run.mjs`), the bundle building, and a\nplayable build. Temporary scaffolding inside a milestone is fine, but nothing temporary survives M8.\n\n**M0: Foundation.**\n- Make the dev folder (§4.1) and fetch the sources (§3.1).\n- `npm install`, then `npx playwright install chromium`. If `/tmp` is full on this shared machine (it was while\n  planning), run Playwright and Chromium with `TMPDIR=<dev>/.tmp`.\n- Write `tools/build.mjs` (concat `src/` into `build/game.js`; bundle `../BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html` per §12).\n- Write `tests/run.mjs` and the headless loader (§11.2); `index.html`; the `00-core` spine (registries, bus, RNG,\n  TUNE); the boot, title and match scene skeletons; the `game.debug` skeleton.\n- Make engine changes 1, 2, 4 and 5 (§3.3) and look at the bat and mitt in the gallery.\n- **Done when:** the bundle opens to a title in `tools/check.mjs` with no errors, the smoke test passes, and the\n  gallery shows a rig holding a bat and wearing a mitt.\n\n**M1: The at-bat** (the core, and the biggest risk; §10 R1 and R2).\n- Field geometry and the Kernel Field TileMap; the Plate Cam with the fence, stands and towers.\n- The pitcher, batter and catcher rigs with clips or fallbacks.\n- Pitch types, windup, release ring, aftertouch; the reticle, swings and contact model; the count rules and calls.\n- Batted-ball physics with home run, foul and fair detection; the Broadcast Cam showing the ball's flight.\n- Umpire stamps, basic sounds, the timing feedback and the dev timing bar.\n- For this milestone only, a ball in play resolves at its landing as a \"HIT!\" or \"OUT!\" stamp by a simple rule. M3\n  replaces this with real fielding.\n- **Done when:** T-PITCH, T-BAT, T-BALL and T-RULES (the count part) pass; at-bats against the CPU are fun in a quick\n  self-play check; Plate Cam screenshots at 1280×720 and 1920×1080 show a readable zone, batter, pitcher and ball.\n\n**M2: The Derby and the AI Hub** (early, to settle the protocol and the bundle; §10 R7 and R8).\n- The Derby: local play with 1–4 players hot seat, targets, scoring, the initials table.\n- `40-hub.js`: connect, our card, ready, start, progress, result, time-up, end, ghosts.\n- The session rules, the meta tags, and the session client placement in the bundle.\n- **Done when:** T-DERBY and T-HUB pass headless and `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true in the real harness for `players=2&auto=1`,\n  `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1` and `&scenario=host-leave`; the bundle still opens normally outside\n  a hub.\n\n**M3: Fielding, running and the full game.**\n- Fielders (assignment, chase, catch, throw, cutoffs, tags, forces, rundowns); baserunners (forces, tag-ups, orders,","numLines":135,"startLine":1677,"totalLines":2123}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XNkmZeRNpdJqNUJRERW5v9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
