{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2wgRwAVzgXh1matJ3p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01N6Wi1qyxYmzggtYvF4pqYN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path('PLAN.md'); s = p.read_text()\nfixes = [\n (\"- **Done when:** T-RULES, T-FIELD, T-RUN and T-AI pass (CPU vs CPU sims in range), and a human vs CPU 3-inning game\\n  plays from start to finish.\",\n  \"- **Done when:** T-RULES, T-FIELD, T-RUN and T-AI pass (CPU vs CPU sims in range), and a 3-inning game with the bot\\n  as player 1 (through the real controls) against the CPU plays from start to finish with no stuck play.\"),\n (\"| core | T-CORE-01..05 | registries; the bus; RNG streams (no `Math.random` in rules: wrap it with a counter during a sim, and it must stay 0 from rules code); determinism; TUNE meta complete (every key has a label, range and default) |\",\n  \"| core | T-CORE-01..05 | registries; the bus; RNG streams; determinism (the same seeded half-inning twice gives the same snapshot hash, and a third run with `Math.random` seeded differently gives the same gameplay hash of score, outs, bases and ball path, which proves the rules never use `Math.random`); TUNE meta complete (every key has a label, range and default) |\"),\n (\"- A determinism check (T-CORE-03) runs the same seeded half-inning twice and compares the hash of its snapshots.\",\n  \"- A determinism check (T-CORE-03) runs the same seeded half-inning twice and compares the hash of its snapshots, then\\n  once more with `Math.random` seeded differently, where the gameplay hash must not change.\"),\n]\nfor old, new in fixes:\n    n = s.count(old); assert n == 1, (n, old[:60])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s); print('ok')\nPY","description":"Fix the M3 check and the determinism test design"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{