compares the hash of its snapshots, then\\n  once more with `Math.random` seeded differently, where the gameplay hash must not change.\"),\n]\nfor old, new in fixes:\n    n = s.count(old); assert n == 1, (n, old[:60])\n    s = s.replace(old, new)\np.write_text(s); print('ok')\nPY","description":"Fix the M3 check and the determinism test design"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01N6Wi1qyxYmzggtYvF4pqYN":{"cwd":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work"}}}
