{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Mk31KdjUKEGmNurxZL6AWt","type":"tool_result","content":"1922\t| rules | T-RULES-01..24 | §6.1 |\n1923\t| pitch | T-PITCH-01..12 | §6.2 |\n1924\t| bat | T-BAT-01..14 | §6.3 |\n1925\t| ball | T-BALL-01..12 | §6.4 |\n1926\t| field | T-FIELD-01..16 | §6.5 |\n1927\t| run | T-RUN-01..14 | §6.6 |\n1928\t| super | T-SUPER-01..10 | §6.7 |\n1929\t| rhubarb | T-RHU-01..06 | §6.9 |\n1930\t| hazards | T-HAZ-01..08 | §6.10 |\n1931\t| ai | T-AI-01..08 | §6.11 (sims in §11.5) |\n1932\t| cams | T-CAM-01..07 | §6.12 |\n1933\t| hud | T-HUD-01..08 | §6.13 |\n1934\t| input | T-IN-01..10 | §6.14 |\n1935\t| talk | T-TALK-01..07 | §6.15 |\n1936\t| audio | T-AUD-01..04 | §6.16 |\n1937\t| crowd | T-CROWD-01..04 | §6.17 |\n1938\t| modes | T-TOUR-01..06, T-TRAIN-01..08, T-DERBY-01..06 | Tour progression, rewards, clubhouse purchases change stats, save and load round-trip; each lesson's pass condition is reachable by its lesson bot; Derby outs, scoring, Golden Balls, targets, the initials table |\n1939\t| mp | T-MP-01..05 | §6.20 |\n1940\t| hub | T-HUB-01..08 | §6.21, with the mock |\n1941\t| attract | T-ATT-01..05 | §6.22 |\n1942\t| dev | T-DEV-01..06 | §6.23 |\n1943\t| ui | T-UI-01..06 | §6.24 |\n1944\t| touch | T-TOUCH-01..03 | §6.26 |\n1945\t| about | T-ABOUT-01..03 | every Source Information field present and non-empty; the four feedback sections present; the version label shows |\n1946\t| playthrough | T-PLAY-01 | §11.4 |\n1947\t\n1948\t### 11.4 The scripted playthrough of the whole game (T-PLAY-01)\n1949\t\n1950\tOne test, run by the bot through the real inputs, with no errors allowed anywhere (`game.errors` empty at every\n1951\tstep) and a time limit of 180 s of real time:\n1952\t1. Boot to the title. Idle 10.5 s: the attract mode starts. Let its whole reel loop once. A tap returns to the title.\n1953\t2. **Spring Training:** all eight lessons, by their lesson bots, each reaching \"LESSON PASSED!\".\n1954\t3. **New Tour in slot 1, with Tour game length Quick:**\n1955\t   - Prologue: advance with ✕.\n1956\t   - Each of the five stops: its pregame, its game, its postgame. In the games the player-1 bot plays at the \"Batzooka\"\n1957\t     level against a Rookie CPU, with the dev cheat \"perfect contact\" on for the bot's side only, so every stop is\n1958\t     won in bounded time.\n1959\t   - After each stop: buy one upgrade in the clubhouse; save.\n1960\t   - Check the scripted Rhubarb at Caldera, the Rally Cap or the boss's short circuit at the MegaDome, the ending and\n1961\t     the credits roll, and the return to the title.\n1962\t4. **Load slot 1** and confirm the Tour is complete and everything is unlocked.\n1963\t5. **Exhibition with four bot players** (two a side) for one inning in a random park; the results screen.\n1964\t6. **Derby** with two hot-seat bots; the initials entry.\n1965\t7. **Hub round** with the mock: card, ready, start, progress, result, end.\n1966\t8. Open the About screen and every page; open the pause menu, then Dev Mode, move a slider, reset it.\n1967\t\n1968\t### 11.5 Balance sims (part of the `ai` suite)\n1969\t\n1970\t- Seeded CPU-vs-CPU 9-inning games at Pro must land in the ranges of T-AI-01: 6 games in the default run, 30 with\n1971\t  `--full` (`M.fast = true` keeps them quick).\n1972\t- Each difficulty pairing: in the default run, the higher level must score more runs in total over 3 seeded games;\n1973\t  with `--full`, it must win at least 60% of 10.\n1974\t- A bot batter against each pitch type: the contact rate is 55–85% at Pro.\n1975\t- The Batzooka's home run rate on contact is 70–95%.\n1976\t- The mean Derby round score of the bot is 1,500–4,000 ft.\n1977\t\n1978\tThese sims only report. The defaults are tuned with them and the sliders in M8, and the ranges stay as tests.\n1979\t\n1980\t### 11.6 Browser checks (`--browser`)\n1981\t\n1982\t- `node tools/check.mjs <bundle>.html` at the default 1280×720, then with `#match`, `#derby`, `#about`, `#gallery`,\n1983\t  then `--size 1920x1080`, and `#touch --size 390x844@3` (the touch-only card). There must be no errors, no external\n1984\t  requests (the bundle is offline), and the canvas covered. Act on every look note.\n1985\t- `tools/filmstrip.mjs` strips (with `--seed 1`, so they repeat) of the swing (contact, power, Batzooka), the pitch,\n1986\t  the throw, the dive, the slide, the wall climb, the umpire calls and the Rhubarb punches. Look at each: wind-up,\n1987\t  strike and settle, with no jerks or backward sweeps.\n1988\t- **Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge.** Look at each:\n1989\t  - the Plate Cam in each park and both batter's boxes;\n1990\t  - the Broadcast Cam on a deep fly;\n1991\t  - the HUD at 1920×1080 (a TV);\n1992\t  - prompts for the pad (PlayStation and Xbox), the keyboard and the mouse;\n1993\t  - the title, Team Select, the Tour Map, the clubhouse, the results, Dev Mode, the About pages;\n1994\t  - the Moonshot Cam;\n1995\t  - each hazard;\n1996\t  - the touch-only card.\n1997\t\n1998\t### 11.7 The AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\n1999\t\n2000\t`tests/hub.mjs` (Playwright):\n2001\t1. Copy the bundle beside `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`, and start `tools/serve.mjs` (127.0.0.1,\n2002\t   port 0).\n2003\t2. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then\n2004\t   require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and print the failing checks if not.\n2005\t3. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `players=2&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`.\n2006\t4. Open the bundle alone to confirm it reaches the title outside a session.\n2007\t5. Stop the server by its PID.\n2008\t\n2009\t---\n2010\t\n2011\t## 12. Packaging and hand-off"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"ca7bd3c7-6f30-4efd-8de7-687abcc323e2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:39:25.697Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work/PLAN.md","content":"| rules | T-RULES-01..24 | §6.1 |\n| pitch | T-PITCH-01..12 | §6.2 |\n| bat | T-BAT-01..14 | §6.3 |\n| ball | T-BALL-01..12 | §6.4 |\n| field | T-FIELD-01..16 | §6.5 |\n| run | T-RUN-01..14 | §6.6 |\n| super | T-SUPER-01..10 | §6.7 |\n| rhubarb | T-RHU-01..06 | §6.9 |\n| hazards | T-HAZ-01..08 | §6.10 |\n| ai | T-AI-01..08 | §6.11 (sims in §11.5) |\n| cams | T-CAM-01..07 | §6.12 |\n| hud | T-HUD-01..08 | §6.13 |\n| input | T-IN-01..10 | §6.14 |\n| talk | T-TALK-01..07 | §6.15 |\n| audio | T-AUD-01..04 | §6.16 |\n| crowd | T-CROWD-01..04 | §6.17 |\n| modes | T-TOUR-01..06, T-TRAIN-01..08, T-DERBY-01..06 | Tour progression, rewards, clubhouse purchases change stats, save and load round-trip; each lesson's pass condition is reachable by its lesson bot; Derby outs, scoring, Golden Balls, targets, the initials table |\n| mp | T-MP-01..05 | §6.20 |\n| hub | T-HUB-01..08 | §6.21, with the mock |\n| attract | T-ATT-01..05 | §6.22 |\n| dev | T-DEV-01..06 | §6.23 |\n| ui | T-UI-01..06 | §6.24 |\n| touch | T-TOUCH-01..03 | §6.26 |\n| about | T-ABOUT-01..03 | every Source Information field present and non-empty; the four feedback sections present; the version label shows |\n| playthrough | T-PLAY-01 | §11.4 |\n\n### 11.4 The scripted playthrough of the whole game (T-PLAY-01)\n\nOne test, run by the bot through the real inputs, with no errors allowed anywhere (`game.errors` empty at every\nstep) and a time limit of 180 s of real time:\n1. Boot to the title. Idle 10.5 s: the attract mode starts. Let its whole reel loop once. A tap returns to the title.\n2. **Spring Training:** all eight lessons, by their lesson bots, each reaching \"LESSON PASSED!\".\n3. **New Tour in slot 1, with Tour game length Quick:**\n   - Prologue: advance with ✕.\n   - Each of the five stops: its pregame, its game, its postgame. In the games the player-1 bot plays at the \"Batzooka\"\n     level against a Rookie CPU, with the dev cheat \"perfect contact\" on for the bot's side only, so every stop is\n     won in bounded time.\n   - After each stop: buy one upgrade in the clubhouse; save.\n   - Check the scripted Rhubarb at Caldera, the Rally Cap or the boss's short circuit at the MegaDome, the ending and\n     the credits roll, and the return to the title.\n4. **Load slot 1** and confirm the Tour is complete and everything is unlocked.\n5. **Exhibition with four bot players** (two a side) for one inning in a random park; the results screen.\n6. **Derby** with two hot-seat bots; the initials entry.\n7. **Hub round** with the mock: card, ready, start, progress, result, end.\n8. Open the About screen and every page; open the pause menu, then Dev Mode, move a slider, reset it.\n\n### 11.5 Balance sims (part of the `ai` suite)\n\n- Seeded CPU-vs-CPU 9-inning games at Pro must land in the ranges of T-AI-01: 6 games in the default run, 30 with\n  `--full` (`M.fast = true` keeps them quick).\n- Each difficulty pairing: in the default run, the higher level must score more runs in total over 3 seeded games;\n  with `--full`, it must win at least 60% of 10.\n- A bot batter against each pitch type: the contact rate is 55–85% at Pro.\n- The Batzooka's home run rate on contact is 70–95%.\n- The mean Derby round score of the bot is 1,500–4,000 ft.\n\nThese sims only report. The defaults are tuned with them and the sliders in M8, and the ranges stay as tests.\n\n### 11.6 Browser checks (`--browser`)\n\n- `node tools/check.mjs <bundle>.html` at the default 1280×720, then with `#match`, `#derby`, `#about`, `#gallery`,\n  then `--size 1920x1080`, and `#touch --size 390x844@3` (the touch-only card). There must be no errors, no external\n  requests (the bundle is offline), and the canvas covered. Act on every look note.\n- `tools/filmstrip.mjs` strips (with `--seed 1`, so they repeat) of the swing (contact, power, Batzooka), the pitch,\n  the throw, the dive, the slide, the wall climb, the umpire calls and the Rhubarb punches. Look at each: wind-up,\n  strike and settle, with no jerks or backward sweeps.\n- **Screenshots only for what scripts can't judge.** Look at each:\n  - the Plate Cam in each park and both batter's boxes;\n  - the Broadcast Cam on a deep fly;\n  - the HUD at 1920×1080 (a TV);\n  - prompts for the pad (PlayStation and Xbox), the keyboard and the mouse;\n  - the title, Team Select, the Tour Map, the clubhouse, the results, Dev Mode, the About pages;\n  - the Moonshot Cam;\n  - each hazard;\n  - the touch-only card.\n\n### 11.7 The AI Hub harness (`--hub`)\n\n`tests/hub.mjs` (Playwright):\n1. Copy the bundle beside `hub/harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js`, and start `tools/serve.mjs` (127.0.0.1,\n   port 0).\n2. Open `harness.html?game=<bundle>.html&players=2&auto=1`. Wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, then\n   require `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`, and print the failing checks if not.\n3. Repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, and with `players=2&scenario=host-leave&auto=1`.\n4. Open the bundle alone to confirm it reaches the title outside a session.\n5. Stop the server by its PID.\n\n---\n\n## 12. Packaging and hand-off","numLines":90,"startLine":1922,"totalLines":2126}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Mk31KdjUKEGmNurxZL6AWt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
