{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016LhCpaqdLjFacLuwtAv89m","type":"tool_result","content":"2015\t## 12. Packaging and hand-off\n2016\t\n2017\t**`tools/build.mjs` writes the single file** `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html`\n2018\tinto this folder (the dev folder's parent), from this template:\n2019\t```html\n2020\t<!doctype html>\n2021\t<html lang=\"en\">\n2022\t<head>\n2023\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n2024\t<script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, unmodified, inlined: the first script, right after meta charset */</script>\n2025\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n2026\t<title>Batzooka Baseball</title>\n2027\t<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Over-the-top arcade baseball: fireball pitches, a rocket-powered bat, wall-climbing catches and bench-clearing rhubarbs.\">\n2028\t<!-- the hub tags of §6.21 -->\n2029\t<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n2030\t</head>\n2031\t<body>\n2032\t<!-- E.bootSplash('BATZOOKA BASEBALL') markup, as the handoff's index.html has it -->\n2033\t<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n2034\t<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n2035\t<script>/* engine/mocap-readable.js + engine/mocap.js + assets/mocap-batzooka.js */</script>\n2036\t<script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n2037\t</body>\n2038\t</html>\n2039\t```\n2040\t\n2041\t**Build rules:**\n2042\t- **Inlined code:** inline each file as is. If one contains `</script` or `<!--`, stop with an error naming the file\n2043\t  and line, and fix the source (don't escape blindly).\n2044\t- **No outside requests:** no CDN and no network; the page works from file://.\n2045\t- **Size:** the bundle is about 1.5–2 MB, which is fine.\n2046\t- **The hub client:** after building, check that the bundle's first `<script>` is the hub client, byte-identical to\n2047\t  `vendor/aihub-session.js`.\n2048\t\n2049\t**Before handing back:**\n2050\t1. Every test is green with `node tests/run.mjs --all`, including the playthrough, the browser checks and the hub\n2051\t   harness.\n2052\t2. No leftovers: `grep -rniE \"TODO|FIXME|XXX|placeholder|lorem|stub|not implemented\" src/` finds nothing, and no\n2053\t   screen, line or button says \"coming soon\".\n2054\t3. The About/Credits screen shows the final Source Information and the three feedback sections, answered honestly (the\n2055\t   number of issues testing caught, how many were critical, the most and least helpful tests; the six engine answers;\n2056\t   the four prompt answers), with \"unknown\" where something can't be confirmed.\n2057\t4. **`exit-interview.json`** sits in this folder beside the .html, in exactly TASK.md's shape, with every value filled\n2058\t   in (§6.27 for `aiHub`). It must parse:\n2059\t   `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`.\n2060\t5. `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` is complete, and the same list is in the engine feedback.\n2061\t6. **The final chat reply** holds the Source Information, the Testing Feedback, the Engine Feedback and the Prompt\n2062\t   Feedback (as TASK.md requires), and a short summary of the game.\n2063\t\n2064\t---\n2065\t\n2066\t## Appendix A: `BZ.TUNE` defaults (the dev sliders)\n2067\t\n2068\t| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n2069\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n2070\t| Pitching | `pitchSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × every pitch's speed |\n2071\t| | `pitchBreak` | 1.0 | 0–2.5 | × break |\n2072\t| | `aftertouch` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × in-flight steering |\n2073\t| | `releaseWindow` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the perfect-release window |\n2074\t| | `staminaDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × stamina cost |\n2075\t| Batting | `swingTiming` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the timing windows |\n2076\t| | `sweetSpot` | 1.0 | 0.4–2.5 | × reticle radii |\n2077\t| | `exitVelocity` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × exit speed |\n2078\t| | `launchSpread` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the launch-angle response to reticle offset |\n2079\t| Ball | `gravity` | 1.0 | 0.3–2.5 | × 520 U/s² |\n2080\t| | `drag` | 0.05 | 0–0.3 | per second |\n2081\t| | `bounce` | 1.0 | 0.3–1.5 | × surface restitution |\n2082\t| | `rollFriction` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × rolling deceleration |\n2083\t| | `wind` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the park's wind |\n2084\t| Players | `runSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × runners |\n2085\t| | `fielderSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × fielders |\n2086\t| | `throwSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × throws |\n2087\t| | `catchRadius` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.5 | × catch reach |\n2088\t| | `turboPower` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the turbo boost |\n2089\t| | `turboDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the drain |\n2090\t| Over the top | `meterGain` | 1.0 | 0–5 | × meter gains |\n2091\t| | `batzookaPower` | 1.6 | 1.0–3.0 | the Batzooka's exit multiplier |\n2092\t| | `rhubarbChance` | 0.4 | 0–1 | chance on a hard HBP |\n2093\t| | `hazardRate` | 1.0 | 0–4 | × hazard frequency |\n2094\t| CPU | `cpuBat` `cpuPitch` `cpuField` `cpuRun` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × CPU skill |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"708825b7-ef23-4499-af9e-674001e2db5c","uuid":"f7162efc-06bc-4fad-9045-5b0e2e88c2fd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:39:48.553Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174819__xcfe199/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 12. Packaging and hand-off\n\n**`tools/build.mjs` writes the single file** `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174819.html`\ninto this folder (the dev folder's parent), from this template:\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<script>/* vendor/aihub-session.js, unmodified, inlined: the first script, right after meta charset */</script>\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Batzooka Baseball</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Over-the-top arcade baseball: fireball pitches, a rocket-powered bat, wall-climbing catches and bench-clearing rhubarbs.\">\n<!-- the hub tags of §6.21 -->\n<style>html,body{margin:0;height:100%;background:#000;overflow:hidden}#screen{width:100%;height:100%;display:block;image-rendering:pixelated;touch-action:none}</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<!-- E.bootSplash('BATZOOKA BASEBALL') markup, as the handoff's index.html has it -->\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script>/* engine/my-3d2dge.js */</script>\n<script>/* engine/mocap-readable.js + engine/mocap.js + assets/mocap-batzooka.js */</script>\n<script>/* build/game.js */</script>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n**Build rules:**\n- **Inlined code:** inline each file as is. If one contains `</script` or `<!--`, stop with an error naming the file\n  and line, and fix the source (don't escape blindly).\n- **No outside requests:** no CDN and no network; the page works from file://.\n- **Size:** the bundle is about 1.5–2 MB, which is fine.\n- **The hub client:** after building, check that the bundle's first `<script>` is the hub client, byte-identical to\n  `vendor/aihub-session.js`.\n\n**Before handing back:**\n1. Every test is green with `node tests/run.mjs --all`, including the playthrough, the browser checks and the hub\n   harness.\n2. No leftovers: `grep -rniE \"TODO|FIXME|XXX|placeholder|lorem|stub|not implemented\" src/` finds nothing, and no\n   screen, line or button says \"coming soon\".\n3. The About/Credits screen shows the final Source Information and the three feedback sections, answered honestly (the\n   number of issues testing caught, how many were critical, the most and least helpful tests; the six engine answers;\n   the four prompt answers), with \"unknown\" where something can't be confirmed.\n4. **`exit-interview.json`** sits in this folder beside the .html, in exactly TASK.md's shape, with every value filled\n   in (§6.27 for `aiHub`). It must parse:\n   `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`.\n5. `ENGINE-CHANGES.md` is complete, and the same list is in the engine feedback.\n6. **The final chat reply** holds the Source Information, the Testing Feedback, the Engine Feedback and the Prompt\n   Feedback (as TASK.md requires), and a short summary of the game.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A: `BZ.TUNE` defaults (the dev sliders)\n\n| Group | Key | Default | Min–max | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Pitching | `pitchSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × every pitch's speed |\n| | `pitchBreak` | 1.0 | 0–2.5 | × break |\n| | `aftertouch` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × in-flight steering |\n| | `releaseWindow` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the perfect-release window |\n| | `staminaDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × stamina cost |\n| Batting | `swingTiming` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × the timing windows |\n| | `sweetSpot` | 1.0 | 0.4–2.5 | × reticle radii |\n| | `exitVelocity` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.0 | × exit speed |\n| | `launchSpread` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the launch-angle response to reticle offset |\n| Ball | `gravity` | 1.0 | 0.3–2.5 | × 520 U/s² |\n| | `drag` | 0.05 | 0–0.3 | per second |\n| | `bounce` | 1.0 | 0.3–1.5 | × surface restitution |\n| | `rollFriction` | 1.0 | 0.3–3 | × rolling deceleration |\n| | `wind` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the park's wind |\n| Players | `runSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × runners |\n| | `fielderSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × fielders |\n| | `throwSpeed` | 1.0 | 0.5–2 | × throws |\n| | `catchRadius` | 1.0 | 0.5–2.5 | × catch reach |\n| | `turboPower` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × the turbo boost |\n| | `turboDrain` | 1.0 | 0–3 | × the drain |\n| Over the top | `meterGain` | 1.0 | 0–5 | × meter gains |\n| | `batzookaPower` | 1.6 | 1.0–3.0 | the Batzooka's exit multiplier |\n| | `rhubarbChance` | 0.4 | 0–1 | chance on a hard HBP |\n| | `hazardRate` | 1.0 | 0–4 | × hazard frequency |\n| CPU | `cpuBat` `cpuPitch` `cpuField` `cpuRun` | 1.0 | 0–2 | × CPU skill |","numLines":80,"startLine":2015,"totalLines":2130}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016LhCpaqdLjFacLuwtAv89m","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
